5 CONT (marriage between Everett Wilson and Jennie Nyman)
1 SEX M
1 _UID 4BAE51BB1CBC62408C777650BDA817AA6E00
1 CHAN
2 DATE 5 OCT 2019
1 NOTE Horace Everett Wilson was presumably named for his uncle of the same na
2 CONC me; he seems to have gone mostly by Everett in his younger years and Ha
2 CONC rry when he was older.  He was born in Marshall, MO, in 1882, but grew u
2 CONC p in Denver, CO, where his family moved when he was still very young.  H
2 CONC e married Rose Lino in 1903 and they had one child (Leonard) in 1904, b
2 CONC efore divorcing in 1907.  I know little of the following years, but he a
2 CONC pparently moved to the Northwest, where he married Jennie Nyman in Coeu
2 CONC r d'Alene, ID, in 1909.  They had known each other in Denver, but I don
2 CONC 't know the details of how they got back together and married.  Harry a
2 CONC nd Jennie later moved to California, but their first two children (Leon
2 CONC ie and Nyman) were born in Washington in 1916 and 1918.  They were in L
2 CONC os Angeles for the 1920 census, and the twins (Clarence and Harry Jr.) w
2 CONC ere born in Santa Monica in 1922.  Harry and Jennie eventually moved to R
2 CONC iverside, CA, and spent the rest of their lives there, though Harry was a
2 CONC way from home a lot in his job as an electrician for the power company.  H
2 CONC e died in 1943 at the age of 60.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a World War I draft registration card for him on Ancestry.com (
2 CONC listed as Everett Wilson).  It gives a physical description: medium hei
2 CONC ght, slender build, blue eyes, brown hair.  It is dated 12 Sep 1918, on
2 CONC ly a couple of months before the end of the war, so I don't know if he a
2 CONC ctually served or for how long if so.  He and Jennie had one child and a
2 CONC nother on the way at that time.  They were living in Seattle, WA, and h
2 CONC is occupation is listed as drayage, which I suppose means he was a truc
2 CONC k driver (or maybe they were still using horse carts).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A newspaper clipping from the Riverside Press sent by Leonie Rinker (Ho
2 CONC race’s older sister) to Leonard Wilson (Horace’s son) after Horace’s de
2 CONC ath reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT WILSON—In Riverside, Calif., May 11, 1943, Harry E. Wilson, aged 60 yea
2 CONC rs. Late resident of 3199 Chestnut street, Riverside, Calif.  Beloved h
2 CONC usband of Mrs. Jennie M. Wilson of Riverside, Calif.  Loved father of C
2 CONC larence R. Wilson of Riverside, Mrs. Leonie Trickey of Maywood, Calif., H
2 CONC arry E. Wilson, Jr., of the U.S. Army and Nyman A. Wilson of San Diego, U
2 CONC .S. Navy, and Leonard Everett Wilson of Denver, Colorado. Also survived b
2 CONC y three grandchildren, Patricia Marie Trickey, Lawrence Robert Wilson a
2 CONC nd Clarence Ralph Wilson. Funeral services will be conducted in the E. H
2 CONC . Preston Funeral Home chapel Friday, May 14th at 2:30 o’clock. Interme
2 CONC nt in Olivewood cem  [rest cut off]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A letter from Leonie Trickey (Horace’s daughter) to Leonard and Betty W
2 CONC ilson after Horace’s death said that “He just coughed and fell off his w
2 CONC ork bench dead.  Mother said he had been feeling better than he has for a l
2 CONC ong time, and Tuesday morning when he went to work he was feeling good, a
2 CONC nd by 4:30 he was gone.  They say he even sat with the fellows and ate h
2 CONC is lunch, but Leonard, he really looked terrible: just skin over his bo
2 CONC nes.”  In agreement with his death certificate, Margaret Henry (Horace’
2 CONC s granddaughter) told me that he was working at Food Machinery (a compa
2 CONC ny).  She said that her father Clarence was also working there at the t
2 CONC ime.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on his death certificate is Harry E. Wilson.  Cause of death i
2 CONC s listed as pulmonary hemorrhage due to pulmonary tuberculosis.  He die
2 CONC d en route to Community Hospital in Riverside, Riverside County, CA.  T
2 CONC he death certificate says he had been in Riverside 20 years and in Cali
2 CONC fornia 25 years before his death.  His occupation is listed as electric
2 CONC ian for Food Machinery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900 census
2 CONT Listed as Horace E. Wilson.  Age 17, born in August 1882.  Born in Miss
2 CONC ouri, both parents born in Missouri.  Attended school (9 months).  Livi
2 CONC ng with his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910 census
2 CONT Image 14 on Ancestry.com (District 0133, Elk Twp., Spokane Co., WA)
2 CONT Listed as Evertt Wilson.  Renting a home with three other men.  Age 28, b
2 CONC orn in Missouri, both parents born in Missouri.  Single.   Occupation, l
2 CONC aborer in a saw mill.
2 CONT This is a good candidate for him, but I can't be certain since he's not w
2 CONC ith a family so there are no other names to check for consistency.  He w
2 CONC as married to Jennie by this time, but maybe they were living apart for s
2 CONC ome reason.  Note that Elk Twp. and Spokane are only about 30 miles fro
2 CONC m Coeur D'Alene, ID, where they were married in 1909.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 census
2 CONT Image 7 on Ancestry.com (District 190, Los Angeles Assembly District 63
2 CONC , Los Angeles Co., CA)
2 CONT Listed as Everett Wilson.  Renting home.  Age 37, born in Missouri, bot
2 CONC h parents born in United States.  Occupation, electrician.  Household c
2 CONC onsisted of Everett, Jennie M., Leonie E., and Nyman A. Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930 census
2 CONT Image 25 on Ancestry.com (District 56, Riverside, Riverside Co., CA)
2 CONT Listed as Harry E. Wilson.  Address, 3882 Tallonay (?) St.  Renting hom
2 CONC e, $85 per month.  They had a radio set.  Age 47, age 24 at first marri
2 CONC age [this isn't right].  Born in Missouri, both parents born in United S
2 CONC tates.  Occupation, electrician for the power company.  Household consi
2 CONC sted of Harry E., Jennie M., Leonie, Nyman, Harry E. [Jr.], and Clarenc
2 CONC e Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1940 census
2 CONT Image 10 on Ancestry.com (Districts 33-50, Riverside, Riverside Co., CA
2 CONC )
2 CONT Listed as Harry E. Wilson, age 56, born in Missouri.  Address, 4044 Len
2 CONC nard (?) Pl.  Renting home, $25 per month.  Completed four years of col
2 CONC lege (?).  Lived in Arlington, Riverside Co., CA, in 1935.  Occupation, e
2 CONC lectrician for electric-power company.  Worked 52 weeks in 1939.  Incom
2 CONC e in 1939, $1508 (?).  Household consisted of Harry E., Jennie M., Nyma
2 CONC n A., Harry E. Jr., and Clarence R. Wilson.
