1 NOTE From the McGrew letter:  "...the first Sandidge came to this country fr
2 CONC om Ireland ... before the Revolutionary War.  She was the daughter of a
2 CONC n Irish nobleman and she eloped with a commoner."  [I don't know of any b
2 CONC asis for this story.]  Also, the letter said that two sons of Leonard a
2 CONC nd Mary died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her name was spelled Mary Sanridge in a letter from Jennie Wilson to Le
2 CONC onard Wilson, 5 Nov 1940.  She is listed as Mary A. Sandridge in the An
2 CONC cestral File and in the Hotchkiss manuscript.  I have seen her called M
2 CONC ollie in a couple of places: in the probate case file of her mother, Ma
2 CONC rie L. Isbell, and in a posting to the Rootsweb Sandidge message board b
2 CONC y Karen Jorgensen dated 2 Aug 2009.
