1 NOTE In a letter from Catherine (Rinker) McGrew and Leonie (Wilson) Rinker t
2 CONC o Michael Wilson dated 16 Nov 1966, they wrote "William Adair & Mary El
2 CONC izabeth Wilson were the parents of nine children, seven of whom were Ca
2 CONC therine, Benjamin, Leonard, Annette, Adair, Byrd, Horace Everett."  Mar
2 CONC y L. was listed in the 1850 census (only 8 months old), but not listed i
2 CONC n the 1860 census, so presumably she died young.  In a letter from Mary E
2 CONC . (Reeves) Wilson to Jeanette (Reeves) Leonard dated 17 Mar 1848 (from t
2 CONC he Abiel Leonard Papers), she mentioned a child named William David; he m
2 CONC ight be another child who died young, born between Leonard and Mary L.  T
2 CONC his would make nine children.  However, In another letter from Mary Wil
2 CONC son to Jeanette Leonard, dated 12 Feb 1856 (also from the Abiel Leonard P
2 CONC apers), she wrote "it has pleased our kind and heavenly Father to take f
2 CONC rom me four dear little ones", so it sounds like Mary had at least 11 c
2 CONC hildren, of whom 4 died young.  And she may have had another one after 1
2 CONC 856 because Mollie Turner Reid said that she had "12 children - some di
2 CONC ed young."  Perhaps three of the children were stillborn and not includ
2 CONC ed in Leonie's count.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In information from Ridge Park Cemetery in Marshall, MO, her cause of d
2 CONC eath is listed as "flux - old age".
2 CONT
