1 NAME Benjamin Harrison /Wilson/
2 GIVN Benjamin Harrison
2 SURN Wilson
1 SEX M
1 _UID 057D15DF6FF41D4691B547F7D7F6C61A6D40
1 CHAN
2 DATE 3 OCT 2019
1 NOTE Author of the Ben H. Wilson letter.  He was obviously named after his g
2 CONC randfather, Benjamin Harrison Reeves.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "History of Saline County, Missouri", he was the captain of compan
2 CONC y F, 7th regiment, Missouri state militia (Union; pp. 278, 288, 350, 48
2 CONC 9).  He was elected circuit clerk in 1866 (p. 359).  In the Marriage Re
2 CONC cords of Saline County, there are lots of marriages performed or record
2 CONC ed by Ben H. Wilson in the period of 1868 to 1870.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some additional information on his military service is available at the w
2 CONC eb site of the Missouri Secretary of State, which has old soldiers’ ser
2 CONC vice cards online (http://www.sos.mo.gov/archives/soldiers/).  The card f
2 CONC or Benj. H. Wilson shows that he enlisted 12 Feb 1862 at Marshall, must
2 CONC ered in on 17 Apr 1862 at Georgetown (Missouri), and mustered out on 22 A
2 CONC pr 1865.  It also has a physical description of him (5' 11½'', dark hai
2 CONC r, hazel eyes, dark complexion), gives his occupation as clerk, and say
2 CONC s he was a native of Fayette, Howard Co., Mo.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Web site of the Missouri Secretary of State also shows B. H. Wilson e
2 CONC lected to the state house of representatives in 1864, with a note that h
2 CONC e resigned (http://www.sos.mo.gov/archives/history/historicallistings/m
2 CONC olegw.asp).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I obtained much more information on Ben's service during the Civil War f
2 CONC rom some descendants of his.  On the Vaughan Family Tree on Ancestry.co
2 CONC m (see http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/41955588/person/19710995147) ther
2 CONC e is a photo of a coat of arms made for him, which contains text summar
2 CONC izing all he did during the war.  The text is not readable in the photo o
2 CONC n the Vaughan site, but I was able to get additional information from D
2 CONC ebbie and Mike Vaughan.  The text follows, with some punctuation added/
2 CONC changed to make it more readable, plus a couple of spelling corrections
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Enlisted as a private, Missouri vols. in Fall of 1861 but not mustered.  E
2 CONC ntered service as private, Missouri Militia volunteers, Feby. 12, 1862.
2 CONC   Appointed and commissioned Captain Co. “F” 7th Regiment Missouri Stat
2 CONC e Militia Cavy. April 17, 1862.  Regiment organized in central Missouri a
2 CONC t Sedalia and Warrensburg and organization completed May 1, 1862.  Duty a
2 CONC t Georgetown till June.  Moved to Syracuse Mo. and duty there till Aug. 1
2 CONC 5.  Detached as provost marshal at Syracuse Mo. June to Aug.  Action at P
2 CONC ink Hill Mo. June 11, Raytown June 28, Pleasant Hill July 11, Columbus J
2 CONC uly 23, Independence Aug. 11.  March to the relief of Lexington Aug. 16
2 CONC –19.  Battle of Lone Jack Aug. 16.  March from Sedalia to relief of Spr
2 CONC ingfield Mo. Aug. 20–27.  Attached to Totten’s Command, S.W. Dist. of M
2 CONC o. Dept. of Mo., to Oct. 1862.  March to Crane Creek Sept. 21–22 and ad
2 CONC vance post duty there till Oct. 13.  Action at McGain’s Ferry Sept. 23.
2 CONC   Detached as judge advocate of a military commission Oct. 1862. — Re-j
2 CONC oined regiment at Crane Creek.  March to Cassville Oct. 13–14.  Attache
2 CONC d to 2-Brig. 3-Div. Army of the Frontier.  Action at Old Fort Wayne Oct
2 CONC . 22, Fayetteville Oct. 24, Oxford Bend Oct. 27–28, Huntsville Oct. 28.
2 CONC   Moved to Cross Hollows.  Thence to Newtonia Nov. 3 and operations fro
2 CONC m that point against Livingston’s guerillas till Dec. 11.  March to Pea R
2 CONC idge Dec. 11–13 and duty there till Jany. 11, 1863.  Campaign against M
2 CONC armaduke.  March to the relief of Springfield Jany. 11–12.  Expedition t
2 CONC owards Hartsville Jany. 13–18.  Moved to Greenfield Mo. Jany. 20.  Duty a
2 CONC t Linden, Christian Co., and Newtonia till Aug.  Action at White River A
2 CONC pril 17, Carthage May 16, Hartsville May 23, Mountain Store May 26, Car
2 CONC thage May 27–28.  Transferred to Central Dist. of Missouri Aug. 1 and d
2 CONC uty there operating against guerillas and bushwhackers till Oct. 1863.  C
2 CONC ampaign against Shelby Oct. 6–18, 1863.  Action at Warsaw Oct. 8, Black
2 CONC water Oct. 12, Lamine crossing Oct. 12.  Comdg. the advance.  Marshall O
2 CONC ct. 12–13, Merrill’s crossing Oct. 13, Jonesboro Oct. 14, capture of Sh
2 CONC elby’s train.  Placed in charge of the prisoners captured by Gen’l. E. B
2 CONC . Brown.  Detached as ordnance officer at Jefferson City Mo. under Gen’
2 CONC l. F. S. Callender Oct. 1863 to Sept. 1864.  Price’s invasion of Missou
2 CONC ri Sept. 29–Oct. 28.  Assigned to duty on staff of Gen’l. Alfred Pleasa
2 CONC nton Sept. and Oct.  Action at Osage River Oct. 6, Morceau Bottom Oct. 7
2 CONC , Boonville Oct. 9–11, California Oct. 10., Boonville Oct. 12–13, Sedal
2 CONC ia Oct. 15.  Duty in ordnance dept. at Jefferson City Mo. till Apr. 186
2 CONC 5.  Mustered out at Warrensburg Mo. and discharged at St. Louis Mo. Apr
2 CONC . 22, 1865.  Commissioned Colonel – Missouri Vol. Militia, but not must
2 CONC ered in because of close of war.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I also obtained from Debbie and Mike Vaughan a transcription of a lette
2 CONC r about family history written by Ben.  The transcription was not dated
2 CONC , but it indicated that the letter was written about 1895.  This letter a
2 CONC nd some notes about it my me can be found at https://archive.org/detail
2 CONC s/BHWilsonLetterWithNotes .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob Reeves had his name as William A. Wilson (I'm pretty sure he got th
2 CONC e info from me, and just mistyped).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry.com has a database called Headstones Provided for Deceased Uni
2 CONC on Civil War Veterans, 1879-1903, which includes images of records from t
2 CONC he National Archives.  There is one for Benj H Wilson, which gives his d
2 CONC eath date as 11 May 1904.  However, his headstone at Riverside Cemetery s
2 CONC hows his death as 10 May 1904 (image on FindAGrave.com).  I have heard t
2 CONC hat the worn headstone was replaced by Harry Powell Wilson Jr. sometime i
2 CONC n the 1980's or 1990's.  Perhaps it was corrected at that time?
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on his death certificate (obtained from Debbie and Mike Vaugha
2 CONC n) is Benjamin Wilson.  Cause of death was cerebral thrombosis.  Died a
2 CONC t the Denver City & County Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 census
2 CONT Listed as Benjamin H. B. Wilson, age 14, born in Missouri.  Attended sc
2 CONC hool within the year.  Living with his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 census
2 CONT Listed as Benjamin Wilson, age 24, born in Missouri.  Occupation clerk.  L
2 CONC iving with his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 census
2 CONT Image 2 on Ancestry.com (Marshall Twp., Saline Co., MO)
2 CONT Listed as B.H. Willson, age 34, born in Missouri.   Occupation, clerk o
2 CONC f court.  Value of real estate listed as $17000, value of personal esta
2 CONC te listed as $3000.  Household consisted of B.H., Olive A., William A., a
2 CONC nd Bernice Willson; Mary E. Willson [Ben's mother], Horace E. and Byrd L
2 CONC . Willson [Ben's brothers]; two apparent boarders, Jacob Vandike and Wm
2 CONC . Johnston, who look like they also worked for Ben in the court clerk's o
2 CONC ffice; E. and Mary Gilmore (domestic servant and her baby); and Henry B
2 CONC ryd, a farm laborer (another boarder?).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 census
2 CONT Image 37 on Ancestry.com (District 66, Marshall, Saline Co., MO)
2 CONT Listed as Ben H Wilson, age 44.  Born in Missouri, father born in Virgi
2 CONC nia, mother born in Kentucky.  Occupation, bank clerk.  Household consi
