1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT Of her [Euphemia Donley's] daughters I have said that Martha married B. H
2 CONC . Reeves, raised a large family, and died in 1835.  Although her educat
2 CONC ion was limited, she was a lady of vigorous mind and performed well her p
2 CONC art in rearing her family and as a member of society.  She was a devote
2 CONC d wife and an affectionate and careful mother, who guided well her nume
2 CONC rous household.  I say numerous, because she had under her care a numbe
2 CONC r of servants as well as children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Benjamin Harrison Reeves and Martha Donley were first cousins
2 CONC .
