1 NOTE Several sources list his birth place as Lincoln County, KY.  Christian C
2 CONC ounty seems more likely, but it is possible that Martha went to be with h
2 CONC er mother in Lincoln County.  The SpenReeve family tree has Christian C
2 CONC ounty, but it also shows his middle name as Lowell; I don't know where t
2 CONC hat is from.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was probably named for William Long, B.H. Reeves' oldest (half) brot
2 CONC her, who died when B.H. was still young.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The SpenReeve family tree shows his death as 5 Dec 1890; it looks like t
2 CONC he years are switched for William and Hannah.  Another note -- John Wan
2 CONC amaker said that William and Hannah Ann were buried in Givens Cemetery n
2 CONC ear Fayette, MO, but Find A Grave (listing for William Long Reeves) cal
2 CONC ls it Patton Cemetery in Fayette, MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT 22 #1690 is rather confusing.  It lists two William Long Reeves's a
2 CONC s marrying Hannah Ann Givens (one is called William Long Reeves II). Th
2 CONC e marriage date of 1831 was given for one of them and the death date of 1
2 CONC 886 was given for the other.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob Reeves says that William was an attorney in Elkton, KY.  That is no
2 CONC t correct.  Perhaps confused with a different William Reeves.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that William Long Reeves and Hannah Ann Givens were first cousins.
