1 NAME Brewer /Reeves/
2 GIVN Brewer
2 SURN Reeves
1 SEX M
1 _UID 2E13E5658560C1458FA4E72711708BDEA1A0
1 CHAN
2 DATE 9 JUN 2020
1 NOTE According to Bob Reeves, Brewer moved to Lincoln County, KY, about 1790 a
2 CONC nd then to Christian County, KY, about 1796 (actually Logan County at t
2 CONC he time).  He settled on the West Fork of the Red River.  He was instru
2 CONC mental in the creation of Christian County from Logan County, which was a
2 CONC pproved in December 1796 and specified to take effect on 1 Mar 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT "History of Todd County, Kentucky" (1884, p. 148) says that "The first a
2 CONC uthentic date of a settlement being made here [Trenton precinct] is tha
2 CONC t of 1796.  In that year Brewer and Martha Reeves came here from August
2 CONC a County, Va."  According to Perrin's "County of Christian, Kentucky: H
2 CONC istorical and Biographical" (1884; obtained from http://www.westernkyhi
2 CONC story.org/christian/perrin/chap2.html), Brewer was one of the first jus
2 CONC tices of the peace for Christian County when it was first organized.  T
2 CONC he act of the Legislature that established Christian County ("An act fo
2 CONC r the division of Logan County") specified that "the Justices to be nam
2 CONC ed in the commission of the peace for said county of Christian, shall m
2 CONC eet at the house of Brewer Reeves, in said county, upon the first court d
2 CONC ay after the said division shall have taken place".  Later, Perrin says "
2 CONC The first court held in the new county convened on the 21st day of Marc
2 CONC h, 1797. Present--Jacob Barnett, Moses Shelby, Hugh Knox, Jonathan Loga
2 CONC n and Brewer Reeves, gents, Presiding Justices of the county."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT It is stated in a biography of great-grandson Adair Wilson (see his not
2 CONC es) that Benjamin H. Reeves' father served in the Revolution.  That is p
2 CONC ossibly true, but I don't have any evidence for it.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There are at least two versions of Brewer's ancestry:
2 CONT
2 CONT One, from James Hotchkiss, is that his father was Henry (d. 1745 in Ess
2 CONC ex Co., VA), mother Jochebed, and he had brothers Henry and John (d. ab
2 CONC t Jun 1799 in Rockingham Co., VA), and sister Mary.  Grandfather and gr
2 CONC eat-grandfather also named Henry (d. 1728/29 in Essex Co., VA, and 1687 i
2 CONC n Essex Co., VA, respectively).  He had Brewer's birth on 22 Nov 1722 i
2 CONC n Spotsylvania Co., VA.  (WFT 137 # 299 has father Henry, mother Jacheb
2 CONC ed, and possibly a brother named John.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The other, from Bob Reeves, is that his father was Thomas (b. abt 1700, d
2 CONC . abt 1760), mother Sarah, and he had brothers Thomas (b. aft 1745) and J
2 CONC ohn (b. abt 1747 in Spotsylvania Co., VA; d. 5 May 1799 in Rockingham C
2 CONC o., VA).  Grandfather was Henry (b. 1665 in Spotsylvania Co., VA; d. ab
2 CONC t 1729 in VA).  He had Brewer's birth on 14 Sep 1745 in Spotsylvania or A
2 CONC ugusta Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Looks like they both have the same grandfather Henry, but different fat
2 CONC hers.  Also, same brother John, but different other siblings.  Note tha
2 CONC t there is a line in Chalkley's Chronicles that mentions that a Thomas R
2 CONC eeves is "brother to Brewer Reeves" (from May 1780).
2 CONT
2 CONT Another possibility that has been raised is that this Brewer may have b
2 CONC een a son of the Brewer born in 1722.  I don't think there's very stron
2 CONC g evidence for this (or for any of the other theories, for that matter)
2 CONC , but it is suggested that the elder Brewer could have died and the you
2 CONC nger Brewer was then raised by Brewer Sr.'s brother Thomas, so that he w
2 CONC as like a brother to Thomas's sons (Thomas and John), but was actually t
2 CONC heir cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Reeves Project (https://thereevesproject.org/data/tiki-index.php?pa
2 CONC ge=Reeves_Brewer_3381; accessed 26 Oct 2019) lists his father as Thomas R
2 CONC eeves Sr., with mother unknown.  (Apparently, identification of Sarah a
2 CONC s Thoms Sr.'s wife might be confusion with Thomas Jr.'s wife, who was k
2 CONC nown to be Sarah.)  They agree with a birth date of 14 Sep 1745.  Some n
2 CONC otes from the Reeves Project:
2 CONT
2 CONT Brewer Reeves is named in Augusta County court records of the 1770's as t
2 CONC he brother of Thomas Reeves; however, the will of Thomas' uncle George R
2 CONC eeves in Spotsylvania County names several children of Thomas Reeves, S
2 CONC r. but not Brewer.  Brewer's brother was definitely Thomas Reeves, Jr. f
2 CONC or he gave a deposition in the case of Herndon vs. Thomas Reeves for sl
2 CONC aves mortgaged to Herndon by Thomas Reeves in Spotsylvania then removed t
2 CONC o Augusta where he sold them.  The deposition of Brewer Reeves in that c
2 CONC ase also mentions Thomas Reeves' wife Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruer Reeves, Benjamin Harrison and John Fitzwater were chosen to value t
2 CONC he lands belonging to sundry landholders of the county.  Rockingham Cou
2 CONC nty, February 18, 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brewer Reeves is listed on the 1784 tax list of Anthony Rader in Rockin
2 CONC gham County, Virginia with 2 white tithes.  As Bruor Reeves, he is agai
2 CONC n listed in Rockingham on the 1789 personal tax lists.
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1784, a petition was presented to the Rockingham County court f
2 CONC or a road from the county line by Plain Mills to Harrisonburg.  Brewer R
2 CONC eeves and others were appointed to make a report, and on July 26 the co
2 CONC mmittee reported on a route for the road.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brewer's brother Thomas Reeves, Jr. migrated to Kentucky a few years be
2 CONC fore Brewer and appeared on the 1792 tax list of Woodford County.  In 1
2 CONC 795, Brewer was also listed along with Thomas on the Woodford County ta
2 CONC x list.  The 1796 list does not include Brewer who appears to have move
2 CONC d on to Christian County where he was one of the earliest settlers.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1797 he was among the first justices of the court in Christian Count
2 CONC y, Kentucky.  He is mentioned repeatedly in William Henry Perrin's Hist
2 CONC ory of Christian County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although there is no will on record in Christian County, Kentucky for B
2 CONC rewer Reeves, Will Book A lists the appraisal of his estate on page 19 [
2 CONC appraisal filed in Christian County Court 29 Nov 1799] and the settleme
2 CONC nt of his estate dated 6 Jun 1804 was recorded in the July term of the C
2 CONC hristian County Court on pages 56 thru 62 of the same book.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Martha Davis of Augusta County, named daughter Martha Rives (
2 CONC sic), December 26, 1805.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: There is much speculation and confusion regarding this family, sp
2 CONC ecifically the children of Thomas Reeves, Sr. of Essex County and later S
2 CONC potsylvania.  The records of Spotsylvania, Frederick and Augusta counti
2 CONC es in Virginia need to be thoroughly researched to document the family c
2 CONC onnections.
