1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otway C. Reeves married and raised a large family.  He died many years a
2 CONC go in Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Todd County, Kentucky, ed. J. H. Battle, F. A. Battey Publis
2 CONC hing Co., 1884, p. 148:
2 CONT
2 CONT ...a third son, Ottaway, was a farmer here for many years.  He was said t
2 CONC o be a man of fine intellect and good education, but did not in any way
2 CONC , as his brothers had done, seek political notoriety.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth in Lincoln County is from Bob Reeves.  I don't know if it's right
2 CONC , but maybe Brewer Reeves and family spent some time in Lincoln County b
2 CONC efore going to Woodford County.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married and raised a large family.     -- WFT 22, 1690
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a lot of guesswork in putting this family together from censu
2 CONC s records, beginning with whether the Mary A. Reeves listed in the 1850 c
2 CONC ensus is Otway's widow, and whether she is also the Mary Reeves living w
2 CONC ith the Bollinger (Bowlinger) family in the 1860 census.  There may be m
2 CONC istakes.  Bob Reeves initially listed Reuben as a child, but not Martha
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT His first name is spelled Otway and Ottaway in different places.  A cha
2 CONC rt by H.F. Hunter Jr. in the Katherine Gentry Bushman Papers, 1961-1997 (
2 CONC Accession 35743, Personal Papers Collection, The Library of Virginia, R
2 CONC ichmond, VA) lists him as Henry Ottaway Reeves.
