1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest daughter [Margaret] of my Aunt Donly married her cousin, W
2 CONC atts D. Ewin, of whom I have occasion to write hereafter.  She was an a
2 CONC miable and affectionate girl, beloved among her cousins, and after marr
2 CONC iage a loving wife and mother.  She was affected by the death of her ol
2 CONC dest son Charles when ten or twelve years old, and her only daughter Eu
2 CONC phemia, when just budding into womanhood.  She survived her husband, an
2 CONC d lived beyond her three score years and ten.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth dates from Bob Reeves and Ancestral File do not fit with the Park
2 CONC s manuscript, because he says that she was the youngest daughter.  The b
2 CONC irth date here is from Daniel Cormode.  Bob Reeves' death year of 1835 d
2 CONC oes not fit with the above statement that she lived over 70 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT 22, 1690 did not have the children's names.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob Reeves' e-mail listed her as Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cormode info listed her as Margaret Donnelly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Watts Davis Ewin and Margaret Donley were first cousins.
