1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Davis the next in succession in the family, (if I mistake not) w
2 CONC as born December 8, 1765.  I can speak of him from my own recollection, h
2 CONC ave been familiar with him from my earliest infancy until near fifteen y
2 CONC ears old; and an inmate of his family and participant of his generous h
2 CONC ospitality and affectionate kindness for more than six months, after I w
2 CONC as a man.  At an early age he married Annie Caldwell, a scion of the go
2 CONC od old Scotch-Irish stock, and worthy of her husband.  They settled at R
2 CONC ed Rock Spring soon after their marriage; and there they lived beloved a
2 CONC nd respected by all who knew them, until separated by her death about t
2 CONC he year of 1835 or ’36.  And he continued to dwell in the same house un
2 CONC til his death at the mature age of eighty-six.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three children, Walter, born in 1791, William Caldwell, 1791, a
2 CONC nd Martha Ann, 1803.  William Davis was a warm hearted, affectionate ma
2 CONC n and particularly so to those of his own kith and Kin.  He had a turn f
2 CONC or public business.  At my earliest recollection he was overseer of the p
2 CONC oor, in which office he continued until late in life.  He was also for m
2 CONC any years justice of the peace, and afterwards High Sheriff of Augusta C
2 CONC ounty.  In these offices he was faithful to his duties, and the poor of t
2 CONC he county went with all of their complaints, as to a father.  He was a k
2 CONC ind neighbor, and hospitable to strangers.  He was remarkable for his a
2 CONC bstemious habits never tasted ardent spirits and detested tobacco in al
2 CONC l of its forms.  He kept a good table, but his own diet was very simple
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Parks (above), he was born on 8 Dec 1765, but "Tinkling Sp
2 CONC ring: Headwater of Freedom", p. 461, says that his gravestone has his d
2 CONC eath at age 86 yrs., 1 mo. and 24 days, which works out to 10 Dec 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived at Rock Spring Farm.   -- WFT 22 # 1690
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT No middle name given in WFT 5 # 1914 and WFT 137 # 229.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT 137 # 299:
2 CONT Supplement to the Annals of Augusta County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Cynthia McBride (e-mail dated 8 Oct 2019), William served a
