1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, my mother, the eighth child of Walter and Martha (C) Davis, w
2 CONC as born September 30th, 1770, married Joseph Parks, a gentleman from Pe
2 CONC nnsylvania, then a resident of Virginia, 24th of July 1795.  Their chil
2 CONC dren were James, born January 11th, 1798, Thomas Davis, Born December 8
2 CONC th, 1799, Philander, born January 28th, 1802, and died in infancy, Walt
2 CONC er Davis, born November 10th, 1803, William Augustus, born February 26t
2 CONC h, 1806, Rebecca Clark, August 8th, 1808, Martha Cunningham, born Novem
2 CONC ber 10th, 1810.  Rebecca C. died September 2nd, 1815, aged seven years.
2 CONC   William A., the 6th of the same month, Joseph Parks moved from August
2 CONC a county, Virginia, to Lincoln County, Kentucky, in the autumn of 1814; u
2 CONC ndetermined whether to settle permanently in the northern or southern p
2 CONC art of the State, remained there until the spring, (1815) went into Mer
2 CONC cer County, then in the spring, of 1816, settled in Christian County on M
2 CONC ontgomery Creek, a branch of the West fork of the Red River, residing t
2 CONC here till his death, September 11th, 1825, from which time his wife Eli
2 CONC zabeth remained a widow till her death in October, 1844, making her hom
2 CONC e with her son James till he removed to Illinois in 1833 or ’34.  She t
2 CONC hen made her home with her daughter Martha, now residing in Hopkinsvill
2 CONC e, Kentucky, till her death.  She was active and helpful while she live
2 CONC d, one of whom it could not be said she outlived her usefulness.
