1 NAME Olive Agnes /Powell/
2 GIVN Olive Agnes
2 SURN Powell
1 SEX F
1 _UID 4F18E7DA6DC9B74185431ECFE12C50C72F65
1 CHAN
2 DATE 10 SEP 2019
1 NOTE James Hotchkiss has her last name as Howell, but the Adair Wilson famil
2 CONC y record gives her name as Olive A. Powell, as well as the Saline Co. b
2 CONC irth register in Missouri Pioneers, County and Genealogical Records, Vo
2 CONC lume X (compiled and published by N. Hodges and Mrs. H. W. Woodruff, Ap
2 CONC ril 1971).  Full name of Olive Agnes (Powell) Wilson is from the listin
2 CONC g for her daughter, Genevieve, in "Woman's Who's Who of America", 1914.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Adair Wilson family record shows the marriage between Ben and Olive i
2 CONC n May 1868.  Ancestry.com (Missouri Marriage Records, 1805-2002) shows a m
2 CONC arriage between Benjamin Wilson and Alice Pouell on 27 May 1868 in Howa
2 CONC rd Co., MO.  They have an image of the marriage book, and the bride's f
2 CONC irst name is definitely shown as Alice; it's not a transcription error.  T
2 CONC his is odd, but I think it must be the marriage of Ben and Olive; there i
2 CONC s no other reasonable record for May 1868.  My only guess is that the p
2 CONC erson entering the information mis-heard "Olive" as "Alice".  Informati
2 CONC on on their divorce was obtained from an online Colorado divorce index t
2 CONC hat is no longer available, but it is now on Ancestry.com at “Colorado D
2 CONC ivorceIndex 1851-1985”.  The divorce was listed as taking place in Denv
2 CONC er County, but Denver County did not exist until 1902, so presumably it w
2 CONC as really Denver, Arapahoe Co., CO.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Vaughan Family Tree on Ancestry.com has Olive's birth date as 21 Ju
2 CONC n 1851.  However, this birth date can’t be right because she is listed i
2 CONC n the 1850 census (Saline Co., MO; she was 9 months old at the time of t
2 CONC he census).  (The Vaughan Family Tree parents and family for Olive agre
2 CONC e with the census listing, but the birth date can’t be right).  She is a
2 CONC lso listed as 11 years old in the 1860 census. Additional evidence that t
2 CONC his is the right Olive Powell in 1850 and 1860 is that she had an older s
2 CONC ister named Emily, and there was an Emily Powell living with Ben and Ol
2 CONC ive Wilson in the 1880 census.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a bit confusing...  She is listed in the 1930 census as Olive E
2 CONC . Goodwin, widow, living with daughter Genevieve Wilson in White Plains
2 CONC , NY (Genevieve listed as a social worker, so it's definitely the right f
2 CONC amily).  They are also listed together in the 1925 New York State censu
2 CONC s, in New York City (listed as Olive A. Goodwin this time).  She is lis
2 CONC ted as Olive A. Goodwin, widow, in the 1920 census in East Orange, NJ, b
2 CONC oarding with the family of Chas. Malloy.  In "History of the Long Islan
2 CONC d College Hospital and Its Graduates" by Joseph H. Raymond (Brooklyn, N
2 CONC Y, 1899, obtained from Google Books), there is a listing for Henry Timr
2 CONC od Goodwin, whose second wife was Olive Agnes Powell of Missouri (marri
2 CONC ed 1894).  They are listed together (she as Olive E. Goodwin) in the 19
2 CONC 00 census in Richmond Co., NY, along with two sons who are presumably f
2 CONC rom Henry's first marriage.  Olive's birth is given as Jun 1852 there, w
2 CONC hich isn't right (she was listed in the 1850 census, see above).  Henry T
2 CONC . Goodwin is listed as divorced in the 1910 and 1920 censuses.  So it l
2 CONC ooks like Olive tended to fib about her age and didn't want to tell peo
2 CONC ple she was divorced.  The Vaughan Family Tree and the CG Miller Family T
2 CONC ree say she died in 1936, but the Benjamin Harrison Wilson family tree s
2 CONC ays 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 census
2 CONT Listed as Olive (?) A. Willson, age 21, born in Missouri.  Living with h
2 CONC er husband, B.H. Willson, and family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 census
2 CONT Listed as Ollive A Wilson, age 31, born in Missouri, father born in Ken
2 CONC tucky, mother born in Louisiana.  Living with her husband, Ben H. Wilso
2 CONC n, and family.
