1 NOTE She apparently had a nickname of Dhu within the family (from letters in t
2 CONC he Leonard Collection of the State Historical Society of Missouri Manus
2 CONC cript Collection).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob Reeves says she lived in Memphis, TN, and then moved as a widow wit
2 CONC h two children to Cincinnati.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Adolph and Mary come from Bob Reeves, who did not have the oth
2 CONC er children.  Edith comes from the 1860 census.  She is not listed with t
2 CONC he family in 1870, but I'm not sure it's the right family listing (John a
2 CONC nd Maria Ainsley, living in Memphis, TN; the children are listed as Ber
2 CONC nard and Meme, which could conceivably be weird spellings for Menard an
2 CONC d Mary).  Eugenia is from the SpenReeve family tree.  I don't know wher
2 CONC e that information is from, but I suppose Missouri could have been in T
2 CONC odd County visiting her brother or something like that.  In the 1900 ce
2 CONC nsus, Missouri Ainslie said she had two living children, which would be A
2 CONC dolph and Mary.  It's hard to read how many children she had had, thoug
2 CONC h; it looks like 2 with 4 written over it.  Four children would fit the f
2 CONC amily as listed here.  The SpenReeve family tree has two other children
2 CONC , Lucy L. and Adelina (actually should be Adelma).  They are from the 1
2 CONC 880 census, but it turns out that they were children of John's brother G
2 CONC eorge Ainslie.  Not sure where George and his wife were in 1880, but ap
2 CONC parently their children were staying with his mother.
