1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha C. Parks, daughter of Joseph and Elizabeth (Davis) Parks was mar
2 CONC ried to Wm. Harvey Moore at the residence of her brother James Parks, i
2 CONC n 1833.  Harvey Moore was a thorough scholar, and had a remarkable memo
2 CONC ry, reciting whole pages from Scott’s and other poems, without an appar
2 CONC ent effort to commit them to memory.  Their children were William H., E
2 CONC lizabeth Davis, Mary Agnes, Thomas Parks, three last dying in childhood a
2 CONC nd youth; Thomas at fifteen, remarkably amiable and intellectual, Walte
2 CONC r, Henry, Martha, Agnes, and Mary Elizabeth.  Henry married, and in 187
2 CONC 9 died at Memphis of yellow fever; Martha Agnes married Mr. Mitchell, a
2 CONC fter a brief year of happiness, died – the beautiful, gifted and accomp
2 CONC lished idol of husband, mother, brothers, and sisters, leaving her infa
2 CONC nt daughter, Agnes, to her sister’s care.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Parks manuscript lists her as Martha Cunningham Parks.  You would t
2 CONC hink he would know his own sister’s middle name, but Bob Dryden lists h
2 CONC er as Martha Augusta Parks.
