1 _UID 34EF47068AAEB946B6B5C8474B5ADBA5465E
1 CHAN
2 DATE 5 FEB 2018
1 NOTE Her maiden name is given as Jennie Marie Nyman on Leonie Trickey's Soci
2 CONC al Security application.  Her name is also listed this way on her death c
2 CONC ertificate.  A birth record on Ancestry.com ("Sweden Indexed Birth Reco
2 CONC rds 1860-1941", obtained from Elaine Cosner) gives her name as Jenny Ma
2 CONC ria with father's name of Nils Nyman.  In that time and place, she migh
2 CONC t have been known as Jenny Nilsdotter, rather than Jenny Nyman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her death certificate gives her birth date as 18 Nov 1885, but the birt
2 CONC h record gives it as 17 Nov 1885.  The place of birth is given as Timrå
2 CONC , Västernorrland, Sweden, in the birth record.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional information obtained from Elaine Cosner:
2 CONT
2 CONT From Canadian passenger lists and Canada-U.S. border crossings, she sai
2 CONC led on the Parisian from Liverpool, England, to Quebec, Canada, in 1896 w
2 CONC hen she was 10 years old.  Her residence was listed as Drontheim.  She w
2 CONC as going to her brother-in-law, Jos Nylander, in Duluth, MN.  Arrival d
2 CONC ate listed as 25 Jul 1896 (I think this is the arrival in Quebec).  Jen
2 CONC ny was accompanied by her mother's sister, Anna Andersen, and her baby.  A
2 CONC nna was going to Chicago to meet her husband, Axel Anderson.  Anna's ag
2 CONC e was listed as 27.  The passenger list says that Anna was Norwegian an
2 CONC d from Drontheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jennie may have lived for a while in an orphanage in Minnesota, but thi
2 CONC s is not certain.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter from Jennie Wilson to Leonard Wilson dated 17 Oct 1940, Jen
2 CONC nie said that "my sister Clara and I were boarding with Mr. Linder next d
2 CONC oor [either to Horace Wilson and his first wife, Rose, or to Rose's par
2 CONC ents; this would be in Denver] and my brother-in-law left milk at Rose’
2 CONC s mother’s every day...".
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on her death certificate is Jennie Marie Wilson.  Immediate ca
2 CONC use of death was pneumonia, but she had ovarian cancer.  Died at Genera
2 CONC l Hospital of Riverside County, Arlington, CA.  Her address is given as 4
2 CONC 538 1st Street, Riverside, CA.  Her parents are listed as Nels Nyman an
2 CONC d ? Sigler.  The death certificate gives length of stay in Riverside Co
2 CONC unty and in California as 36 years, which would go back to about 1924.  N
2 CONC ote that Horace and Jennie were in Los Angeles for the 1920 census, so t
2 CONC here seems to be an inconsistency.  The responses on Horace's death cer
2 CONC tificate work out to living in California since about 1918 and in River
2 CONC side County since about 1923, which is consistent with the 1920 census.  S
2 CONC ince Nyman was born in Washington late in 1918, they probably moved to C
2 CONC alifornia in 1919.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 census
2 CONT Listed as Jennie M. Wilson, age 34, born in Sweden, both parents born i
2 CONC n Sweden.  Immigrated to U.S. in 1896, naturalized in 1907.  Living wit
2 CONC h her husband, Everett Wilson, and children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930 census
2 CONT Listed as Jennie M. Wilson, age 44, age 21 at first marriage [I don't t
2 CONC hink that is right], born in Minnesota [I don't think that is right], f
2 CONC ather born in Germany [I don't think that is right], mother born in Swe
2 CONC den.  Living with her husband, Harry E. Wilson, and children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1940 census
2 CONT Listed as Jennie M. Wilson, age 53, born in Sweden.  Naturalized citize
2 CONC n.  Completed four years of high school.  Lived in Arlington, Riverside C
2 CONC o., CA, in 1935. Living with her husband, Harry E. Wilson, and children
2 CONC .
