1 SEX M
1 _UID 537F6024B6DC7C489FEC0B653F3AD4D2C6DC
1 CHAN
2 DATE 16 JUN 2020
1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Donly lived at Burksville, Kentucky, till after his marriage with M
2 CONC iss Martha Stockton, a most excellent lady, who died within less than t
2 CONC wo years after giving birth to their only child, a son.  He never marri
2 CONC ed again, but spent his time alternately in Missouri and Kentucky, unti
2 CONC l his son had arrived at manhood he settled in Texas, where he died, at w
2 CONC hat time I am not informed.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Some family trees say he was born in Cumberland County, KY, but that se
2 CONC ems unlikely.  From the Parks manuscript, Lincoln County seems more lik
2 CONC ely, and Find A Grave (listing for James D Donley) says Lincoln County a
2 CONC nd shows that on his gravestone.  The Bakers of Cumberland Co., Ky fami
2 CONC ly tree says that he died in Rusk County, Texas, but I think that is a m
2 CONC istake.  Son Stockton lived in the town of Rusk, Cherokee County, at th
2 CONC at time, and that is where James is buried.  So I am assuming that Jame
2 CONC s died in or near the town of Rusk.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was likely James Davis Donley, named for his uncle James Davis.  We k
2 CONC now that, like his three sisters, James went to Missouri relatively ear
2 CONC ly.  We don’t know just when he went, but he was in Adair County, Kentu
2 CONC cky, in July 1819 when he was married, and then was in Missouri by May 1
2 CONC 821 when son Stockton was born in Howard County.  WFT 22 # 1690 said th
2 CONC at he went back to Kentucky in 1833 (see the notes for Stockton Patsey D
2 CONC onley; actually it said that he and Stockton went to Kentucky in 1933, b
2 CONC ut presumably that was supposed to be 1833).  His whereabouts in the 18
2 CONC 40 census is not known; there was a James Donly in Gallatin County, Ken
2 CONC tucky, in 1840, but that one is listed as age 30–40, which is too young
2 CONC .  He is listed in the 1850 census in Cumberland County, Kentucky.  Dr. P
2 CONC arks says that he spent his time alternately in Missouri and Kentucky, s
2 CONC o perhaps he went back and forth multiple times.  And then we know he w
2 CONC as in Texas (probably Cherokee County) in 1858 when he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT A number of  family trees show a daughter Frances who was born about 18
2 CONC 16.  The origin of this seems to be that James D. Donley was living wit
2 CONC h Frances Munson and her family in the 1850 census in Cumberland County
2 CONC , KY.  Given that 1816 is three years before James and Martha married a
2 CONC nd given that Dr. Parks said James had only one child, I am not going t
2 CONC o include Frances here.  It seems entirely possible that James was livi
2 CONC ng with an unrelated family and people have wrongly inferred a relation
2 CONC ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, some family trees show three younger children: Anne, Mary, and Wi
2 CONC lliam.  However, I believe they were children of James' brother William
2 CONC .  See the notes for Mary A. Stuart (William's wife).
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 AUG 1788
2 PLAC Lincoln Co., KY
