1 NOTE From the Parks manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Donly carried on the tanning business in Russellville, Kentucky f
2 CONC or some time successfully, during which time he married Mary Stuart, ni
2 CONC ece of his brother James’ wife, and also of Judge Archibald Stuart of S
2 CONC taunton, Virginia.  She was a beautiful and amiable young lady and made h
2 CONC im an excellent wife.  He was married in 1820.  There was a great strug
2 CONC gle then in Kentucky business circles.  It was the time of Commonwealth p
2 CONC aper, etc., and not many years afterwards he found it necessary to chan
2 CONC ge his business.  He moved to Cumberland County and about the year of 1
2 CONC 830 or 1831 was killed by the falling of a large beam connected with so
2 CONC me machinery which he and his wife’s uncle were erecting at Salt Works.
2 CONC   He left several children, the oldest not more than ten years old, wit
2 CONC h their young mother.  Their subsequent history I have not learned.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a tanner in Russellville, KY.    -- WFT 22, 1690
