1 _UID 76CADDD37FC7DD4E9E7ED01806300548E898
1 CHAN
2 DATE 30 MAY 2020
1 NOTE "Settlers by the Long Grey Trail:  Some Pioneers to Old Augusta County, V
2 CONC irginia, and Their Descendants, of the Family of Harrison and Allied Li
2 CONC nes", by J. Houston Harrison (Joseph K. Ruebush Co., Dayton, VA, 1935; r
2 CONC eprinted by C. J. Carrier Co., Harrisonburg, VA, 1983), p. 361:
2 CONT
2 CONT This Robert [Harrison] was born in Rockingham, in August 1783, and died i
2 CONC n Christian County, Kentucky, June 17, 1853, aged 69 yrs. 10 mo.  He ma
2 CONC rried there, April 11, 1811, Sally Davis, the daughter of James Davis, s
2 CONC on of Walter and Martha (Cunningham) Davis, and granddaughter of Robert C
2 CONC unningham, of Augusta, who with Col. John Willson, served as a first Bu
2 CONC rgess of the county.  She died Dec. 29, 1861.  Their children were -- N
2 CONC aomi (m. Wm. H. Forston), Sarah, Martha, Debora (m. Geo. Fortson, bro. o
2 CONC f Wm.), Davis, William, and Fayette, (b. Mar. 15. 1815, d. Paduach, Ky.
2 CONC , 1897.)  The last named married October, 1838, Harriette, the daughter o
2 CONC f James Bradshaw, of Christian County, Ky, and had -- James H., Mary El
2 CONC izabeth, Robert B., William D., Gustavus, Edward, Elbridge B., and Sall
2 CONC y; of whom Mary Elizabeth, b. July 1841, m. Aug. 4, 1864, William Boase T
2 CONC rewolla.  (From data kindly supplied by Rev. James A. Trewolla, of Brad
2 CONC dock, Pa., a grandson of the last named, through his son Charles. B.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a lot of confusion about Robert Harrison and his family.  To b
2 CONC egin with, Settlers by the Long Grey Trail, on p. 361, starts discussin
2 CONC g Robert Harrison who was a son of Zebulon Harrison and Margaret Craven
2 CONC s.  It is stated that he inherited land from his grandfather, Capt. Rob
2 CONC ert Cravens, in 1761 and he was appointed a constable in 1779.  It says t
2 CONC hat his wife’s name was uncertain, but may have been a daughter of Will
2 CONC iam Young, who mentioned “Him who was my son-in-law Robert Harrison” in h
2 CONC is 1810 will.  Then, at the bottom of p. 361 is the paragraph above, wh
2 CONC ere it starts talking about Robert Harrison who was born in August 1783
2 CONC , died on 17 Jun 1853, and married Sally Davis.  This can’t be the same a
2 CONC s the Robert Harrison at the top of the page, because that one was born b
2 CONC efore 1761.  There is no transition saying that this Robert Harrison is t
2 CONC he son of the other Robert Harrison, but that is apparently implied.  O
2 CONC ne bit of evidence that there were two Robert Harrisons is that an imag
2 CONC e on the Trewolla Moskop Haas Mansfield Tree web site of an agreement d
2 CONC ated 10 Mar 1813 for William C. Davis (Sallie’s brother) to sell 667 ac
2 CONC res of land to Robert Harrison Sr. also has a signature of R. Harrison J
2 CONC r. as a witness.
2 CONT  
2 CONT The basis for the birth and death dates of this Robert Harrison appears t
2 CONC o be a bible page stating “Robert Harrison Sen Died June 17th 1853 Aged 6
2 CONC 9 years 10 months”, an image of which is also on the Trewolla Moskop Ha
2 CONC as Mansfield Tree web site.   Notes on the site explain that the “Sen” i
2 CONC s to distinguish this Robert Harrison from Robert Benjamin Harrison (a g
2 CONC randson), who is listed right below him.  However, there is also a deat
2 CONC h record at “Kentucky, Death Records, 1852-1953” on Ancestry.com, which s
2 CONC hows the death of Robert Harrison on 16 Jun 1853, age70, parents Zebulo
2 CONC n and Margarett Harrison.  This is surely the same Robert Harrison even t
2 CONC hough the date is different by one day and the age says 70 instead of 6
2 CONC 9.  An age of 70 doesn’t fit at all for someone who was a son of Zebulo
2 CONC n Harrison and Margaret Cravens.  It’s at least theoretically possible f
2 CONC or him to be a son of Zebulon (born 1718), but not of Margaret Cravens (
2 CONC born 1724).  So, were the parents listed wrong—did they list his grandp
2 CONC arents for some reason?  Or was the age listed wrong?  This seems unlik
2 CONC ely given that it basically matches the bible record.  The earlier Robe
2 CONC rt Harrison, born before 1761, would have been at least 92 in 1853.  He
2 CONC re it is assumed that the bible record is the most reliable.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is of interest to note that, according to various family trees (incl
2 CONC uding the Trewolla Moskop Haas Mansfield Tree), Zebulon Harrison was a f
2 CONC irst cousin of Jane Harrison, who married Daniel Smith (parents of the S
2 CONC mith brothers who married Margaret and Martha Davis).
2 CONT  
2 CONT Most sources just list him as Robert Harrison.  The middle initial T is f
2 CONC rom Diane’s Genealogy web site (http://dgmweb.net/genealogy/FGS/D/Davis
2 CONC James-DeborahMiller.shtml, downloaded 20 Feb 2007).  She has a transcri
2 CONC ption of a gravestone (I think) that says:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sallie Harrison
2 CONT daughter of James Davis and
2 CONT wife of Robert T. Harrison
2 CONT December 16, 1790 - December 29, 1861
2 CONT aged 71 years
2 CONT
