1 NOTE "History of Saline County, Missouri", Missouri Historical Co., St. Loui
2 CONC s, 1881, p. 854:
2 CONT
2 CONT From biography of John B. Davis:  James R. is a member of the present c
2 CONC ounty court of Saline county, a position he has held before, and which h
2 CONC is father held before him.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hillis/Abney/Franklin/Smith AWT site gives his middle name as Robin
2 CONC son, but information from Robert Davis gives it as Robison.  The Reed F
2 CONC amily Tree and Find A Grave also have Robinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A letter from James R. Davis to a cousin, dated 10 Jun 1868, Longwood, P
2 CONC ettis Co., MO (from the Missouri History Collection, Missouri History M
2 CONC useum, St. Louis, MO; transcription obtained from Russell Reed):
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Cousin
2 CONT  
2 CONT I have looked for a letter from you for a long time but have not receiv
2 CONC ed a line from any of our friends for a long time.  We heard Aunt Rebec
2 CONC ca was dead and I suppose it is time but no one has informed us of it a
2 CONC s yet that we knew it was [MS illegible]  I have written to you twice s
2 CONC ince the war but have not received any answer yet to any of my letters  w
2 CONC e are all well  Mother is living with me an has tolerable health for he
2 CONC r age.  Shelton has moved to Morgan County and all the balance doging a
2 CONC round  Politically we are under the nig but never can be socially for I d
2 CONC etest negro equality an any of its kindred is nig and all of the advoca
2 CONC tes of such abominable nonsense  a white negro is meaner than the black o
2 CONC ne but [MS illegible] [MS illegible] in that.  Charlotte ought to have s
2 CONC omething coming to her from Fathers estate but it is said we made it al
2 CONC l to Peter Steele  if we did it was not intended to be done  we did not s
2 CONC ell him interest in the property reserved for her.  Father [?] I would b
2 CONC e glad if you would get a lawyer to look at the deed we made Peter Stee
2 CONC le and if anything can be made take the proper course to make it.  I do n
2 CONC ot want to pay anything to a lawyer unless he can make the money out of C
2 CONC harlotte interest there and if you can get one to take it on that way p
2 CONC lease do so.  Give my respect to cous Wil + Family uncle Jacob and all f
2 CONC riends and write to me.  Mother is very anxious to hear from you all te
2 CONC ll uncle Jacob to write and Will and let my [me?] hear from all ours & C
2 CONC lahorn and Moore before another war commences  all join me in Respects t
2 CONC o you and all
2 CONT  
2 CONT Your Cousin
2 CONT  
2 CONT Jas R. Davis
2 CONT  
2 CONT Have you all moved the grave yard  cousin Will said they intended to do s
2 CONC o and did he move our babe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell Reed makes the following identifications:  Aunt Rebecca refers t
2 CONC o Rebecca Van Lear Davis, who died in September 1867.  Mother is Sallie V
2 CONC an Lear Davis.  Shelton is Shelton S. Abney, James’ brother-in-law.  Ch
2 CONC arlotte is Charlotte Steele Davis, James’ wife.  The reference to Fathe
2 CONC rs estate refers to John David Steele, Charlotte’s father.  Peter Steel
2 CONC e is Charlotte’s brother.  And Uncle Jacob is Jacob Van Lear Jr., broth
2 CONC er of Rebecca and Sallie Van Lear.  The notes about illegible manuscrip
2 CONC t are from Russell Reed.]
