1 CHAN
2 DATE 19 AUG 2020
1 NOTE "History of Saline County, Missouri", Missouri Historical Co., St. Loui
2 CONC s, 1881, p. 854:
2 CONT [From biography of John B. Davis] Jacob C. has filled several important o
2 CONC ffices in Illinois; was a member of congress, and also in the state leg
2 CONC islature, while quite a young man.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_C._Davis):
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Cunningham Davis (September 16, 1820 – December 25, 1883) was a p
2 CONC olitician, a U.S. Representative from Illinois.  He was one of five men t
2 CONC ried and acquitted in Illinois of the murder of Joseph Smith, founder o
2 CONC f the Latter Day Saint movement.
2 CONT  
2 CONT Political life
2 CONT  
2 CONT Born near Staunton, Virginia, Davis attended the common schools and the C
2 CONC ollege of William & Mary, Williamsburg, Virginia.  He moved to Warsaw, I
2 CONC llinois, in 1838, where he studied law.  He was admitted to the bar and c
2 CONC ommenced practice in Warsaw.  He served as clerk of Hancock County, Ill
2 CONC inois.  He was appointed circuit clerk in 1841.
2 CONT  
2 CONT He was elected and served in the Illinois Senate from 1842 to 1848 and a
2 CONC gain from 1850 until his resignation in 1856, having been elected to Co
2 CONC ngress.
2 CONT  
2 CONT Davis was elected as a Democrat to the Thirty-fourth Congress to fill t
2 CONC he vacancy caused by the resignation of William A. Richardson.  He serv
2 CONC ed from November 4, 1856 to March 3, 1857.  He was defeated in his bid f
2 CONC or re-election.  After his defeat, Davis resumed the practice of law in C
2 CONC lark County, Missouri.  He died in Alexandria, Missouri, December 25, 1
2 CONC 883.  He was interred in Mitchell Cemetery, near Alexandria, Missouri.
2 CONT  
2 CONT Murder trial
2 CONT  
2 CONT In 1844, Davis was indicted and tried for the murders of Joseph Smith a
2 CONC nd Hyrum Smith.  The Smiths had been imprisoned in Carthage Jail when t
2 CONC he prison was stormed by an armed mob that shot and killed them.  As a c
2 CONC aptain in command of the Warsaw Rifle Company of the Illinois militia, D
2 CONC avis was accused of having ordered his men to storm the prison.  At tri
2 CONC al, Davis and four other defendants were found by a jury to be not guil
2 CONC ty of the murders.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There is more about the death of Joseph Smith at https://en.wikipedia.o
2 CONC rg/wiki/Death_of_Joseph_Smith, but nothing about Jacob Davis’s involvem
2 CONC ent except that he was tried and acquitted.  It is noted that “The tria
2 CONC l jury was composed exclusively of non-Mormons after the defense counse
2 CONC l convinced the judge to dismiss the initial jury, which included Mormo
2 CONC ns.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Parks manuscript gives his name as Jacob Van Lear (Davis).
