2 CONC fice he now holds.  He also follows farming and stock raising and now o
2 CONC perates 1340 acres of well improved land in Howard County, and 320 acre
2 CONC s in New Mexico.  Since 1920, Dr. Givens has lived in Fayette.  He is a D
2 CONC emocrat and a member of the Methodist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1881 Dr. H. K. Givens married Miss Nannie D. Duncan, and to this uni
2 CONC on the following children were born:  Mary L., teacher, Rockford, Ill.; C
2 CONC . E., the subject of this sketch; Donly, lives in Kansas City, Mo.; Flo
2 CONC rence, married James S. Prosser, St. Louis; Fannie, married W. G. Lockr
2 CONC idge, Richmond township, Howard County; and Willie, married W. L. Talbo
2 CONC t, assistant cashier of The Farmers and Merchants Bank of Fayette.   Dr
2 CONC . Givens has served as curator of Howard-Payne College for 42 years and s
2 CONC ecretary of the board for 32 years and served as president of the board f
2 CONC or 20 years, resigning that office in 1922.  Dr. Givens is an influenti
2 CONC al and highly respected citizen of Howard County.
2 CONT
2 CONT C. E. Givens received his education in the public schools and attended C
2 CONC entral College for two years.  He then became connected with the Farmer
2 CONC s and Merchants Bank of Fayette as bookkeeper, which office he held unt
2 CONC il 1913, when he was appointed assistant cashier.  Mr. Givens is now ca
2 CONC shier of the bank.  He owns a retail and wholesale lumber yard at Glasg
2 CONC ow, and also an interest in 400 acres of land.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 8, 1908, C. E. Givens married Miss Ruth Smith, a native of Fay
2 CONC ette, and the daughter of Solon and Elizabeth (Crews) Smith, the former a n
2 CONC ative of Kentucky and the latter of Richmond township.  Mrs. Smith is t
2 CONC he daughter of Dr. Crews, a sketch of whom appears in this volume.  Mr. a
2 CONC nd Mrs. Smith had six children, of whom Mrs. Givens is the youngest[.]  S
2 CONC he was educated at Howard-Payne College and at Christian College in Col
2 CONC umbia.  Mr. and Mrs. Givens have two children, Margaret and Ruth.
2 CONT
2 CONT In politics, Mr. Givens is a Democrat and he has held the office of cit
2 CONC y council for four years.  He is a member of the Methodist Church and b
2 CONC elongs to the Fayette Commercial Club.  Mr. Givens has served in the of
2 CONC fice of cashier of the Farmers and Merchants Bank of Fayette in a very e
2 CONC fficient manner, and he has an extensive acquaintance in Howard County.  H
2 CONC e stands high in his community.
