1 NOTE "History of Chariton and Howard Counties, Missouri", T. B. Smith and P. S
2 CONC . Gehrig, Historical Publishing Co., 1923, pp. 454-55:
2 CONT
2 CONT From biography of C. E. Givens (his grandson):  C. E. Givens was a nati
2 CONC ve of Kentucky and came to Missouri with his parents, Joseph W. and Mar
2 CONC y Givens.  C. E. Givens became a prominent farmer and stockman, as was h
2 CONC is father, and owned large tracts of land.  He died in 1907, at the age o
2 CONC f 75 years[.]   He was a member of the Methodist Church.  Mary Ann (Kri
2 CONC ng) Givens was born in Fayette and died in 1912 at the age of 70 years.  S
2 CONC he was the daughter of Henry W. Kring, well known jeweler of Fayette an
2 CONC d among the first merchants of the town.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT 22 # 1690:
2 CONT He owned a large farm and raised tobacco and did a large business in ho
2 CONC gsheads.  He was a slave owner, having about 100 when the Civil War sta
2 CONC rted. He lost his cattle, horses and mules in the war.  He rebuilt his f
2 CONC arm and a feew years after the war was running 500 head of cattle and o
2 CONC ther livestock.  He owned 3500 acres.  He took title to the farm on Apr
2 CONC il 25, 1868 from his sister Keziah Givens Johnson.
2 CONT He was the twin of Robert Alexander who died in 1825.
2 CONT He was in complete sympathy with the Confederacy and gave material aid t
2 CONC o it and to its soliders.  He was crippled and thus prevented from join
2 CONC ing the Confederate Army.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Middle name is Ewin in WFT Vol. 22, Tree 1690, but Edwards in the DAR d
2 CONC atabase on Ancestry.com.  The DAR submitter was his daughter (Frances), s
2 CONC o you would think it would be right, but Find A Grave lists him as Char
2 CONC les Ewin Givens and has a picture of his gravestone with that name on i
2 CONC t.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, note that the biography of C. E. Givens the grandson says that th
2 CONC is C. E. Givens was born in Kentucky and his parents were Joseph W. and M
2 CONC ary Givens, which is not correct.  He did have children named Joseph W. a
2 CONC nd Mary Givens, who may be getting mixed up somehow.  Another problem w
2 CONC ith the biography -- Mary Ann Kring is listed as dying in 1912 at age 7
2 CONC 0, which is not correct.
