1 NOTE From the Park manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT By her [mother's] request, Jeannetta was sent to Virginia to be educate
2 CONC d under the care of her aunt Smith.  But when Jeannetta arrived, Aunt S
2 CONC mith too was dead, and her son Daniel Smith took charge of her educatio
2 CONC n.  He sent her to a celebrated school at Winchester where she remained o
2 CONC ne or two years, and returning to Augusta, made her home with Uncle Wil
2 CONC liam Davis, until she married Edward Hall, son of Maj. Alexander Hall, a
2 CONC nd nephew of Judge Archibald Stuart, who brought her to Kentucky, and t
2 CONC hey settled on her mother’s old farm where they raised their family.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first name is spelled Jeannette, Jeannetta, Jennetta, and Jenette i
2 CONC n various places.  Her last name is spelled Ewin or Ewing in various pl
2 CONC aces.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT 22 # 1690:
2 CONT Her mother was very sick so she was taken as a young girl by her cousin
2 CONC , Benjamin Reeves, to her Aunt Margaret.  Margaret died before Jeanette c
2 CONC ould reach her.  Jeannette's mother died about the same time. She was t
2 CONC aken in by Daniel Smith, her cousin.  After marriage she lived in Chris
2 CONC tian or Todd Co., KY.
