1 NOTE The Adair Wilson family record says he was from Memphis, TN.  The 1860 c
2 CONC ensus says he was born in England, but in what seems to be his listing i
2 CONC n the 1870 census, his birth place is given as Kentucky (another reason t
2 CONC o question that 1870 listing, but on the other hand there are often err
2 CONC ors in census listings).  Find A Grave (listing for John Ainslie) also s
2 CONC ays he was born in England.  The location within England is from the Sp
2 CONC enReeve family tree site.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Find A Grave he died from tuberculosis.  His parents were J
2 CONC ohn A. Ainslie and Mary Susannah Borron Ainslie Hogan.  J.S.C. Hogan wa
2 CONC s her second husband, and John and Missouri were living with the Hogans i
2 CONC n the 1860 census.  Missouri and her children were also living with Mrs
2 CONC . Hogan in the 1880 census (Mary Hogan and Missouri Ainslie were both w
2 CONC idows, though Missouri is marked as single in the census).
