1 NOTE History of Todd County, Kentucky, ed. J. H. Battle, F. A. Battey Publis
2 CONC hing Co., 1884, pp. 300-301:
2 CONT
2 CONT DR. JOHN O. McREYNOLDS, of Elkton, Todd County Ky, is one of the promin
2 CONC ent physicians of southern Kentucky and was born in Appomattox County, V
2 CONC a., November 30, 1827; he descends from Scotch-Irish ancestors, who wer
2 CONC e first represented in the United States by James and John McReynolds w
2 CONC ith their widowed mother.  They settled in Pennsylvania, but soon after r
2 CONC emoved to Virginia, from whence have emanated the numerous families of t
2 CONC hat name.  The parents of Dr. McReynolds, James C. and Mary B. McReynol
2 CONC ds, emigrated to Kentucky in 1833, settling in Trigg County, where they d
2 CONC ied, the mother in 1837, and the father in 1844.  In 1846, John O. came t
2 CONC o Elkton, Todd County, and studied medicine under Dr. James A. McReynol
2 CONC ds; entered the Jefferson Medical College of Philadelphia in 1847; grad
2 CONC uated therefrom in 1849 and at once entered upon the practice of his pr
2 CONC ofession in Elkton, where, with slight exceptions he has since practice
2 CONC d; he enjoys the confidence of a large circle of friends, who appreciat
2 CONC e him for his many manly qualities, as well as for his ability as a phy
2 CONC sician.  He has been twice married, first to Miss Julia P. Gorin in 185
2 CONC 3, who died the same year; second, in 1859 to Miss Ellen, daughter of C
2 CONC lark Reeves, who has borne him four children, viz.: Mary B., wife of hi
2 CONC s partner, Dr. Zarecor; James C., a law student in the University of Vi
2 CONC rginia; Robert P. and Ellie R. McReynolds.  Dr. McReynolds is an Elder i
2 CONC n the Christian Church of Elkton, and one of its oldest members.
