1 NOTE "County of Christian, Kentucky. Historical and Biographical", ed. Willi
2 CONC am Henry Perrin, F. A. Battey Publishing Company, 1884 (obtained from G
2 CONC oogle Books), p. 449:
2 CONT
2 CONT HENRY H. BOLLINGER was born in Todd County, Ky., February 1, 1847, and r
2 CONC emoved to Christian County in 1870, where he at present resides.  His f
2 CONC ather, Henry Bollinger, Sr., was born in Maryland, and came to this cou
2 CONC nty in an early day, where he died January 24, 1861.  He first settled i
2 CONC n that portion at present included in Todd County.  Subject's mother, M
2 CONC artha Reeves, was born in Todd County, Ky.  She was the sister of Judge R
2 CONC eeves, an eminent jurist of Texas.  She was married to subject's father a
2 CONC bout 1845.  To the father were born: Eliza (Massie), Katie (Sargeant), H
2 CONC enry H., Reuben R., Jennie A. (Quarles), Madison M. and Lute O. (Hunter
2 CONC ).  Subject was married in 1868, to Miss Annie T., daughter of James Je
2 CONC nkins, of Tennessee, and to them were born two children: Howard M. and H
2 CONC arry R.  Subject is a farmer, and is owner of 225 acres of very fertile l
2 CONC and, on which he has been very successful.  He is a member of the order o
2 CONC f A. F. & A. M.; in religion he is a Cumberland Presbyterian, and in hi
2 CONC s political affiliations a Democrat.
