1 NOTE Full name is from a chart by H.F. Hunter Jr. in the Katherine Gentry Bu
2 CONC shman Papers, 1961-1997 (Accession 35743, Personal Papers Collection, T
2 CONC he Library of Virginia, Richmond, VA).  With the chart was this short p
2 CONC ersonal note:
2 CONT
2 CONT LUTE OTTAWAY BOLLINGER
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandmother Hunter (1861 - 1944) was a frequent summer visitor at our h
2 CONC ome in Trenton.  Mother and Dad Hunter occasionally used this opportuni
2 CONC ty to take a few days vacation, leaving my brother Lee (Bud) and me wit
2 CONC h Grandmother.  Bud and I did not especially look forward to these occa
2 CONC sions.  Grandmother was a product of a strict Swiss heritage and of aus
2 CONC tere times.  For her, summer was the time to collect and preserve garde
2 CONC n produce for leaner days ahead: when Mother and Dad disappeared, bushe
2 CONC ls of tomatoes, beans and corn arrived on our back porch to be peeled, s
2 CONC trung, shucked, washed and cooked.  She was also fond of soup, which we h
2 CONC ad for lunch and supper on a regular basis without variation.  At this t
2 CONC ime she was some 70 years of age and probably considered her grandsons t
2 CONC o be lazy and slothful, but she never complained.
