1 NOTE Mr. and Mrs. Perry Spencer were the ones who donated many (most?) of th
2 CONC e papers in the Abiel Leonard collection of the Historical Society of M
2 CONC issouri Manuscript Collection, formerly the Western Historical Manuscri
2 CONC pt Collection, Columbia, MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Wanamaker manuscript:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanette Spencer was the daughter of Reeves and Alice (Gardenhire) Leon
2 CONC ard.  She was six years old when her father died in 1878.  Alice later m
2 CONC arried Reeves’s younger brother, Nathaniel William Leonard, sometime be
2 CONC tween 1880 and 1900.  The couple and Jeanette continued living at Oakwo
2 CONC od.  Alice died 24 August 1922.  Jeanette had married Richard Perry Spe
2 CONC ncer in 1904.  When William’s health began to fail the couple moved bac
2 CONC k to Oakwood to care for him.  “Mr. Willy” died in 1937.  The Spencers c
2 CONC ontinued living at Oakwood, as did some of their children and grandchil
2 CONC dren.  Perry died in 1953, Jeanette in 1958, both buried in the Fayette c
2 CONC ity cemetery.
