1 NOTE "The Book of St. Louisans", Second Edition, ed. Albert N. Marquis, A. N
2 CONC . Marquis & Co., Chicago, IL, 1912, pp. 564-565 (obtained from Google B
2 CONC ooks):
2 CONT
2 CONT SPENCER, Richard Perry, lawyer; born, Ashland, Boone Co., Mo., Jan. 11, 1
2 CONC 874; son of Richard and Annie (Gibbs) Spencer; graduated from Windsor H
2 CONC igh School, 1891; attended Central College, Fayette, Mo.; married, Faye
2 CONC tte, Feb. 14, 1901, Jeannette Leonard; children: Jane, William Leonard.  P
2 CONC rincipal public schools at Moberly, Mo., 1893-95, at Marshall, Mo., 189
2 CONC 5-97; engaged in practice of law since 1897, having been city counselor o
2 CONC f Marshall, 1897-1903; came to St. Louis, January, 1903, and has since b
2 CONC een engaged here in general practice.  Appointed, August, 1911, by Gove
2 CONC rnor Hadley, Democratic member Board of Election Commissioners of St. L
2 CONC ouis and its secretary (was one of six endorsed by Democratic State Cen
2 CONC tral Committee).  Southern Methodist.  Member St. Louis Bar Association
2 CONC , Missouri State Bar Association and American Bar Association.  Mason (
2 CONC Royal Arch); member Knights of Pythias.  Office: 1212-1220 Central Nati
2 CONC onal Bank Bldg.  Residence: 5520 Cabanne Ave.
