2 CONT
2 CONT BEN REEVES DIED FROM AUTO ACCIDENT INJURIES
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben Reeves died Wednesday afternoon, the result of injuries received in a
2 CONC n auto wreck early Monday morning, the direct cause being septic mening
2 CONC itis.  At the time of going to press no funeral arrangements have been m
2 CONC ade.
2 CONT
2 CONT The accident happened between Fairfax and Craig [Mo.] about four o’cloc
2 CONC k Monday morning, and Paul Reeves [his cousin, grandson of B.P. Reeves] w
2 CONC as at the wheel.  The car left the pavement on level ground and crashed i
2 CONC nto a large electric light pole, breaking it off at the base.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben was taken to a St. Joe hospital where his injuries were cared for a
2 CONC nd he returned to Hamburg about noon Tuesday.  It was not thought that h
2 CONC is condition was serious until Wednesday morning, when he took a sudden c
2 CONC hange for the worse.  Ben’s nose was smashed badly and he had an injury t
2 CONC o his leg and some bruises.  His companion, Paul Reeves, was only sligh
2 CONC tly injured.  The car was badly wrecked by the impact but not a glass w
2 CONC as broken.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben Reeves was a popular young man in the community, and had under his c
2 CONC harge large farm interests.  He leaves his parents, Mr. and Mrs. E.S. R
2 CONC eeves and two sisters, Mrs. A. R. Wanamaker and Mrs. Jack Good to morn [
2 CONC sic] his sudden departure.
