2 CONT obituary, The Hamburg (IA) Reporter, Thursday, September 9, 1926
2 CONT
2 CONT Hamburg was all excitement on Sunday evening when the news flashed abou
2 CONC t town that John Callahan had killed Myron Reeves at the Williams garag
2 CONC e on lower Main street. Callahan, a man some fifty-five years of age an
2 CONC d Reeves, aged thirty seven, had not been on friendly terms for several y
2 CONC ears and during the past few weeks, prior to the shooting, had had more t
2 CONC rouble. Eye witnesses to the shooting stated that Callahan was on the s
2 CONC treet near the garage when Reeves and another man drove up. Callahan, i
2 CONC t was stated, drew his pistol and started shooting at Reeves. The latte
2 CONC r ran into the Williams garage and his pursuer continued shooting, two o
2 CONC f the shots striking Reeves. One shot lodged in his shoulder and as he t
2 CONC urned another struck him in the mouth, lodging in the bones at the back o
2 CONC f his neck. He died almost instantly. Callahan was placed under arrest a
2 CONC nd taken to the county jail at Sidney to await trial for murder. Myron R
2 CONC eeves, son of Mr. and Mrs. B. P. Reeves, was born near Hamburg on Decem
2 CONC ber 31, 1888 and died in Hamburg on September 5, 1926, aged 37 years 9 m
2 CONC onths and 4 days. The deceased was survived by his wife, three sons, on
2 CONC e daughter and his parents. Funeral services were held from the home of h
2 CONC is parents on Wednesday afternoon and interment was made in the Hamburg c
2 CONC emetery.
