2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary E. Wilson Passed Away Last Night At Fruita
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary E. Wilson passed away last night at the Whitehouse hotel at F
2 CONC ruita where she had made her home for the past 12 years.  She had been i
2 CONC n failing health for some time.  Mrs. Wilson was the widow of the late B
2 CONC yrd Wilson of the Gridell and Wilson store at Fruita.  He died about a y
2 CONC ear ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in LaSalle, Ill., on March 12, 1869, Mrs. Wilson was 62 years of a
2 CONC ge.  With her husband she took up residence in Fruita in 1921 at the Wh
2 CONC itehouse hotel.
2 CONT
2 CONT A surviving daughter, who resides in Wyoming, will be in Fruita for the s
2 CONC ervices, to be held at 2 o'clock Friday afternoon at the Starks-DeYarma
2 CONC n chapel at Fruita.  Rev. Edwin Elder will officiate.  Burial will be i
2 CONC n Elmwood cemetery beside her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1910 census says she had only one child.  She was previously marrie
2 CONC d to Samuel H. Elbert in about 1886, and she had a daughter named Evely
2 CONC n Frances Elbert from that marriage.  The 1900 census says she had no c
2 CONC hildren, and Evelyn is not living with her and Byrd; perhaps Evelyn was l
2 CONC iving with her father.  I don’t think that Byrd and Mamie had children t
2 CONC ogether.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on her death certificate is Mary E. Wilson.  Cause of death is l
2 CONC isted as uremia.  Her parents are listed as Arthur Ryall and Mary E. Ki
2 CONC lbourn.
2 CONT Headstone says Mary E. Wilson, 1869 - 1933
