2 CONT Weymouth Jane "Sister" (Martin) Reeves, died peacefully Friday morning, M
2 CONC ay 23rd at Life Care Center of Raynham at the age of 92. She was born i
2 CONC n Stoughton on April 26, 1916, the daughter of the late Branch Woodruff M
2 CONC artin and Lydia Atherton (Hodges) Martin. Mrs. Reeves graduated from St
2 CONC oughton High School and attended Simmons College in Boston to study Jou
2 CONC rnalism. Jane married the late Charles Humphries Reeves and lived in Ne
2 CONC w Orleans and Memphis. After his death she and her two children returne
2 CONC d to Massachusetts and lived in Weymouth. Mrs. Reeves wrote and publish
2 CONC ed company newsletters of two Zenith wholesale distributors, Shobe and N
2 CONC ortheastern, and became the Sales Promotion Manager at Northeastern Dis
2 CONC tributors. She was a member of the Old South Union Church for 60 years. J
2 CONC ane is survived by her daughter, Lynn Reeves Thayer and her husband, Ri
2 CONC chard Thayer of Middleboro and her son, Robert D. Reeves, II and his wi
2 CONC fe, Lee Ann S. Reeves of Gainesville, Florida, six grandchildren, six g
2 CONC reat-grandchildren and several nieces and nephews. A Funeral Service wi
2 CONC ll be held at 1 p.m. on Tuesday, May 27 at the Old South Union Chapel, 2
2 CONC 5 Columbian St., S. Weymouth. Arrangements are made by the C. C. Shephe
2 CONC rd Funeral Home, 134 Pleasant St. (Columbian Sq.), S. Weymouth.
