1 NOTE Posting to OK-OBITS-L mailing list by Don Brownlee on 3 Aug 2000:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ventura County (CA) Star, 3 August 2000:
2 CONT
2 CONT Donley L. Ewin, 88, of Ventura, died July 31, 2000, after a lengthy ill
2 CONC ness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don was born Oct. 3, 1911, in Beggs, Okla. He moved to California with h
2 CONC is family in 1922. He was a 41-year Ventura County resident. Don was a s
2 CONC alesman for Helms Bakery for 33 years. He also worked for Security Firs
2 CONC t National Bank, where he met Betty Early, his future bride. Don and Be
2 CONC tty were married for 63 wonderful years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don enjoyed camping, traveling and golf but most of all, he enjoyed his l
2 CONC oving family. Don was a member of the Ventura Breakfast Lions Club and F
2 CONC irst United Methodist Church, where he was very active.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don will be dearly missed by his family and friends. He is survived by h
2 CONC is loving wife, Betty; daughter and husband, Ann and Dan Cormode; son a
2 CONC nd wife, Ray and Sheila Ewin, all of Ventura; daughter-in-law, Barbara E
2 CONC win of Lafayette, Calif.; sister, Mary Neighbors of Dayton, Nev.; seven g
2 CONC randchildren and their spouses; and nine great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his son, Dick Ewin; sisters, Mildred Amos a
2 CONC nd Florence Ewin; and parents, Robert Donley and Jennie Ewin.
2 CONT
2 CONT A celebration of the life of Don Ewin will be held at 1 p.m. Saturday, A
2 CONC ug. 5, at First United Methodist Church with the Rev. Walter Dilg offic
2 CONC iating.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family requests that, in lieu of flowers, memorial donations be mad
2 CONC e to First United Methodist Church, 1338 E. Santa Clara St., Ventura, C
2 CONC A 93001.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are under the direction of the Ted Mayr Funeral Home, Vent
2 CONC ura.
