1 NOTE Ventura County Star, 19 May 2017 (obtained from Legacy.com):
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Elizabeth "Betty" Ewin(1917 - 2017)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ventura, CA
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Elizabeth ""Betty"" Ewin passed away peacefully on May 15, 2017, at t
2 CONC he age of one hundred in Ventura, California.  She was born in Centrali
2 CONC a, Missouri on March 4, 1917 to Albert Earle and Erma Crawford Early.  S
2 CONC he had an older brother, Raymond and sister, Dorothy.
2 CONT Betty moved to Long Beach in 1930.  The massive 1933 Long Beach earthqu
2 CONC ake, which destroyed Long Beach Poly High School, forced Betty to compl
2 CONC ete her senior year in a tent.  While working as a bank teller, she met a
2 CONC nd married Donley Lyle Ewin in 1936.  Don and Betty had three children, D
2 CONC ick, Ann and Ray.  The family lived in Culver City until 1959, when the
2 CONC y moved to Ventura.  Betty worked for Security Pacific Bank and started a r
2 CONC egional Escrow Service Center for Bank of America.  She retired in 1979
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Betty was especially close with her family and the families of her sist
2 CONC er, Dorothy.  Don and Betty enjoyed camping and visited Yosemite almost e
2 CONC very year for about four decades.  After she retired, they traveled in t
2 CONC heir van for ten weeks seeing sites throughout the United States and vi
2 CONC siting friends and family.  She was a longtime active member of the Uni
2 CONC ted Methodist Church of Ventura.  She celebrated her 100th birthday sur
2 CONC rounded by sixty members of her loving family on March 4th.  She was an i
2 CONC nspiration to all and deeply loved.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband Don and elder son Dick preceded her in death.  She is survi
2 CONC ved by daughter and son-in-law, Ann and Dan Cormode; son and daughter-i
2 CONC n-law, Ray and Sheila Ewin; daughter-in-law, Barbara Ewin; grandchildre
2 CONC n, Scott and Genie Cormode, Cathy and Mark Carriger, Kirste and Tom Ric
2 CONC hards, Derek and Diana Ewin, Michael and Kerrie Cormode, Marci and John W
2 CONC orthy, Alisa and Matt Anderson; great grandchildren, Elizabeth Cormode, D
2 CONC onley Cormode, Maegan Carriger, Melissa Carriger, Rebecca Cormode, Sien
2 CONC a Worthy, Drew Worthy, Kyle Anderson, Jason Anderson, Alex Ewin, Domini
2 CONC c Ewin, Nicolle Richards and Jessica Richards; and great-great granddau
2 CONC ghter, Emma Ewin.
2 CONT
2 CONT There will be a memorial service Saturday, June 17, 2017, 2:00 pm at Te
2 CONC d Mayr Funeral Home, 3150 Loma Vista Road, Ventura.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, a donation may be made to the Salvation Army in Bet
2 CONC ty Ewin's name.
2 CONT Arrangements are under the direction of the Ted Mayr Funeral Home.
