1 _UID 128D6201C6753C419DB287FBC77CF46E3079
1 CHAN
2 DATE 28 SEP 2019
1 NOTE WFT 137 # 299:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fayette Harrison, aka Lafayette Harrison was Harriet Laphand Trewolla's t
2 CONC hird husband.  He was born March 15, 1815 and died August 28, 1897 in P
2 CONC aducah, McCracken County, Kentucky.  He is buried at the Harrison famil
2 CONC y plot on the Old Fate Trewolla farm in LaMont, McCracken County, Kentu
2 CONC cky.  His first wife was Harriett Bradshaw, daughter of James Bradshaw.  H
2 CONC arriet died on April 27, 1889 leaving land and money to her nieces and n
2 CONC ephews.  the bulk of her estate went to her husband, Fayette Harrison w
2 CONC ith the provision that he should see after her sister, Anna Marie Kelle
2 CONC y, and should her husband died before his sister, then the estate would g
2 CONC o to her sister.  This area then became known as the Kelley Community.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Christian County, KY Census, District #2, reel M432-196, page 372B
2 CONC , enumerated August 20, 1850 by John W. Wallace
2 CONT 1-197-206 Harrison, Fayette 34, m, farmer, KY
2 CONT      (remarks: handwritten page #744)
2 CONT 2-197-206 Harrison, Harrit, 30, F, KY
2 CONT 3-197-206 Harrison, James H., 10, M, KY
2 CONT 4-197-206 Harrison, Mary E., 9, F, KY
2 CONT 5-197-206 Harrison, Robert, 8, M, KY
2 CONT 6-197-206 Harrison, William D., 6, M, KY
2 CONT 7-197-206 Harrison, Gustavus, 4, M, KY
2 CONT 8-197-206 Gerel, Robert Y, 19, M, overseer, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wilks & Related Families Pedigree Chart dated October 14, 1993 comp
2 CONC iled by James D. Wilks Jr of Anaheim, California
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Group Sheet of Fayette Harrison and Harriet Bradshaw sent to me b
2 CONC y James D. Wilks Jr. of Anaheim, California
2 CONT
2 CONT History and Families of McCracken County, Kentucky 1824-1989:  FAYETTE H
2 CONC ARRISON, was born March 15, 1815 in Christian County, Kentucky.  His fa
2 CONC ther Robert Harrison, a Virginian by birth settled in Christian County i
2 CONC n 1811 and married Sallie Davis April 8, 1811.  Robert operated a grist m
2 CONC illin connection with his farm and ws thus engaged until his death in 1
2 CONC 852.  Robert's wife, Sallie Davis was the daughter of James Davis and D
2 CONC eborah Miller of Virginia, the granddaughter of Walter Davis and Martha C
2 CONC unningham of Augusta County, Virginia.  Robert and Sallie had eight chi
2 CONC ldren.  Those known are: Fayette, Sarah C., and Martha A. Harrison. Fay
2 CONC ette worked in his father's mill and on the farm until his marriage to "
2 CONC Harrie" Bradshaw in October 1838.  He served two years as postmaster at P
2 CONC embroke, Kentucky where he also kept in partnership with a brother in a g
2 CONC eneral store.  In 1856 he purchased 1,000 acres of land in Ballard Coun
2 CONC ty and 250 acres in McCracken County, where he moved his family to resi
2 CONC de.  Fayette and Harrie had nine children, seven boys and two girls. Th
2 CONC ose known are:  James H., Mary E., Gustavus, Wm. Davis (W.D.) and Rober
2 CONC t Harrison.  Fayette's wife Harrie died in 1876 and he married Mrs. Har
2 CONC riet L. Enders, a lady of large estate and reputed generosity. Fayette w
2 CONC as a member of the F.&A.M. and the IOOF and served as magistrate for tw
2 CONC o years.  He died in August 23, 1897.  Fayette's son, W. D. Harrison bo
2 CONC rn October 1844 served in the Civil War.  He was married June 19, 1879 t
2 CONC o Mallie E. Hopson of Paducah, daughter of George and Nellie Enders Hop
2 CONC son.  Her father was a native of Trigg County, Kentucky.  IN 1880 W.E. p
2 CONC urchardsed 283 acres of land in Ballard county and moved there to rear h
2 CONC is family.  W.D. was a successful farmer, acquiring several hundred acr
2 CONC es of land, part of church and cemetery.  To this union were born eight c
2 CONC hildren:  Mary Emma married to Gillum Aus Chandler; Jackson Fayette mar
2 CONC ried Lola Mae Elrod; Angie M. married George Cook; Lucille married Lex R
2 CONC agland; Jennie, Louis, Elbridge and Antoinette.  W.D., and Mallie wereP
2 CONC resbyterians and W.D.  cast his first presidential vote for H. Seymour i
2 CONC n 1868.  (submitted by Howard E. Randle, grandson of Gillum Aus and Mar
2 CONC y Emma Harrison Chandler and the great great grandson of Fayette Harris
2 CONC on).
