1 NOTE WFT 137 # 299 gives her birth year as 1811 (see below).  The Trewolla M
2 CONC oskop Haas Mansfield Tree gives it as 1815.  Find A Grave (listing for H
2 CONC arriet L Trewolla Harrison) has 1816 and has a picture of her graveston
2 CONC e, which is hard to read but looks like it says 1816.  Furthermore, 181
2 CONC 6 fits better with marriage of her parents in 1815, as given by WFT 137 # 2
2 CONC 99.  Her place of burial is spelled Bauld Knob Cemetery in some places, b
2 CONC ut is listed as Bald Knob Cemetery in Find A Grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT 137 # 299:
2 CONT
2 CONT Harriett Laphand Trewolla was born in England on April 15, 1811 and may h
2 CONC ave come to America with her father, Samuel Pearce Trewolla, prior to 1
2 CONC 818.  She was first married to James L. Owen.  He had acquired a large t
2 CONC ract of land very early in McCracken County, Kentucky when land was sel
2 CONC ling for less than $1.00 per acre.  When Mr. Owen died, Harriet was the p
2 CONC rincipal heir to the extensive lands in the area westward from the Heat
2 CONC h Community.  Included in this plantation was a large house boasting th
2 CONC e only spiral staircase and galvanied bathtub in Western Kentucky. Harr
2 CONC iet was a dynamic woman of an unusual degree, being more than equal to t
2 CONC he rugged demands of the developing frontier.  She was the first Trewol
2 CONC la to arrive in Western Kentucky. After Mr. Owen died, she married Robe
2 CONC rt Enders, a riverboat gambler, who after returning from each trip on t
2 CONC he Ohio River, would pour gold coins into her lap. Harriet's third marr
2 CONC iage was to Lafayette (Fayette) Harrison, a widower in 1885.  Fayett wa
2 CONC s born March 15, 1815 an[d] died August 28, 1897 in Paducah, McCracken C
2 CONC ounty, Kentucky.  Buried at the Harrison Family Plot on the Old Fate Tr
2 CONC ewolla Farm in Lamont, McCracken County, Kentucky.  His first wife was H
2 CONC arriett Bradshaw, daughter of James Bradshw. Harriet died on April 27, 1
2 CONC 889 leaving land and money to her nieces and nephews.  The bulk of her e
2 CONC state went to her husband, Fayette with the provision that he should se
2 CONC e after her sister, Anna Marie Kelley, and should her husband die befor
2 CONC e her sister, the estate would go to her sister.  This area then became k
2 CONC nown as the Kelley Community. Her will was probated May 1889.  Harriet i
2 CONC s buried at Bauld Knob Cemetery off Kelley Road in McCracken County, Ke
2 CONC ntucky. Another researcher has her name as Harriet Lavina Trewolla and h
2 CONC er year of birth as 1815.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Group Sheet of Samuel Pearce Trewolla and Maria Lapham sent to m
2 CONC e by James D. Wilks Jr. of Anaheim, California (shows Harriet Lavina Tr
2 CONC ewolla instead of Harriet Laphand Trewolla)
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Harriet L. Harrison:
2 CONT I, Harriet L. Harrison, of McCracken County, State of Kentucky, being o
2 CONC f sound mind and disposing memory, do make this my Last Will and Testam
2 CONC ent, hereby revoking all former will made by me.
2 CONT 1st.  I will and bequeath to Wm. R. Hapson, the piece of land lying bet
2 CONC ween Frank Kelly and John Ware including the Graveyard, containing sixt
2 CONC y-five acres more or less.
2 CONT 2nd. I will and bequeath to Mary E. Harrison, four hundred dollars to b
2 CONC e paid by my Executor out of my estate.
2 CONT 3rd.  I will and bequeath to George Hapson, four hundred dollards to be p
2 CONC aid by my Executor out of my estate.
2 CONT 4th.  I will and bequeath to Mary Ophella Harrison, daughter of Wm. D. H
2 CONC arrison, two hundred dollars,
2 CONT watch chain and finger ring.
2 CONT 5th.  I will and bequeath to my Husband, Fayet Harrison, his life time, m
2 CONC y house and four hundred acres of land including the land that my dwell
2 CONC ing house is on.  This is for him to see after and care for my sister, M
2 CONC rs. An Kelly and should my husband, Fayet Harrison die before Mrs. An K
2 CONC elly, my sister, then my dwelling and the four hundred acres that I hav
2 CONC e willed to my husband, Fayet Harrison, is to be my sister's, Mrs. An K
2 CONC elly's and her death, it shall be sold and divided equally among her ch
2 CONC ildren.
2 CONT 6th.  I will and bequeath to my husband, Fayet Harrison his lifetime, a
2 CONC ll the furniture in my dwelling house with household and kitchen appert
2 CONC inances(?)
2 CONT 7th.  I will and bequeath to Mrs. Sue Megginson, twenty five acres of l
2 CONC and including the house that she now lives on.
2 CONT 8th.  I will and beqeath to my Niece, Alice V. Ireland, one hundred acr
2 CONC es of land her life time, at her death, it shall be sold and the procee
2 CONC ds divided equally between her brothers and sisters, but this is in no w
2 CONC ay to keep her from sharing with her brothers and sisters in theother p
2 CONC art of my estate.
2 CONT 9th.  I will and bequeath to my Nephew, Walter Kelly, five hundred doll
2 CONC ars or propery equivalent to five hundred dollars in order to make him e
2 CONC qual in my estate to his brothers and sisters.
2 CONT 10th. The remainder of my Estate, I will to be sold, all of my landed e
2 CONC state and stock to be sold and the proceeds , divided equally between m
2 CONC y sisters, An M. Kelly's children, viz:  Mrs. Delia F. Hill, Mrs. Alice V
2 CONC . Ireland, Mrs. Cora D. Craig, Theodore J. Kelly, Mrs. Ida Chiles, Fran
2 CONC kl H. Kelley, George W. Kelley, Walter E. Kelly, and Clara Kelly.
2 CONT Article 11.  I will all my notes (promissory) and money to be equally d
2 CONC ivided between my sister, An. M. Kelly's children, this is my Last Will i
2 CONC n witness of this will,  I hereby fix my name and seal this the 3rd day o
2 CONC f January 1889.
2 CONT H. L. Harrison (signed)
2 CONT witness:  C.H. Brothers & W.B. Trewolla
2 CONT State of Kentucky - County of McCracken
2 CONT
2 CONT "History & Families of McCracken County, Kentucky 1824-1989", page 258: T
2 CONC rewollas, Kelleys and Hills:
2 CONT The Trewollas, Kelleys and Hills came from England to Virginia about 18
2 CONC 41. ..... part of McCracken Co., KY which was known as the "Kelley comm
2 CONC unity".  In the late 1800s Harriet Trewolla and her sister Anna Marie, b
2 CONC oth daughters of Samuel and Rowena Laphand Trewolla, moved from Virgini
2 CONC a with a number of other relatives to McCracken County, KY.  Anna Marie w
2 CONC as born in Richmond, VA in 1818 and died in McCracken County in 1894.  S
2 CONC he married David Allen Kelley who was born in Virginia in 1810 and died i
2 CONC n McCracken County in 1880.  Harriet was born in England apr. 11, 1811 a
2 CONC nd died in McCracken County in 1889.  After she moved to McCracken Coun
2 CONC ty she married Edward Owen, who had purchased a vast are of land which e
2 CONC xtended from South of Lamont and North to Metropolis Lake, for less tha
2 CONC n a dollar an acre.  Since Harriet had no children, her estate was left t
2 CONC o her husband.  At his death it was to go to her sister Anne Marie and h
2 CONC er 13 children.  Harriet Laphand Kelley (1836-1859), Adelia Frances Kel
2 CONC ley (1837-1917), John S. Kelley (1841-1853), David J. Kelley (1843-1862
2 CONC ), Alice V. Kelley (1844-?), Cora D. Kelley (1846-?), Theodore L. Kelle
2 CONC y (1848-?), Ida Blanche Kelley (1850-1916), Charles Pearce Kelley (1853
2 CONC -?), Edward O. Kelley (1855-1865), George W. Kelley (1858-?), Walter L. K
2 CONC elley (1861-?).  Anna Marie and David's second daughter, Adelia Frances K
2 CONC elley, married Francis Marion Hill who was born August 11 in Appomattox C
2 CONC o., VA, died January 28 at Lamont, in McCracken County.  They had eight c
2 CONC hildren:  John married Bell Blanks, Eddie who married Elizabeth Trewoll
2 CONC a, A.P. who married Onie Moody, Barnett who married Mattie Mulvin, Walt
2 CONC er who married Cecil Cockrell, Mary who married Lee Ray, Sue who marrie
2 CONC d William Megginson and Katie who married Robert Emerson Williams.  All o
2 CONC f their children, except John who raised his family in Paris, AR, raise
2 CONC d their families in the Heath and Lamont Communities.  Katie Hill, youn
2 CONC gest daughter of Adelia Frances and Francis Marion married Robert E. Wi
2 CONC lliams.  They had seven children:  Stratton married Florida Pugh, Henri
2 CONC etta married Miles W. Meredith, Ed married Edna Zottarelle, Marion marr
2 CONC ied George G. Houston, Bill married Zelma Sharp, Mildred married Willar
2 CONC d Carroll, Katie married J. D. Merryman.  In the will of Harriet 1889 s
2 CONC he also left a plot of ground on the Kelley Road in Western McCracken C
2 CONC ounty known as "Bauld Knob Cemetery" for the final resting place for th
2 CONC e families of the Trewollas, Kelleys and Hills.  You will also fina a n
2 CONC umber of Hills, Kellys, and Trewollas on the headstones in the McKendre
2 CONC e United Methodist Church Cemetery in Western McCracken County, KY.  Ma
2 CONC rion W. Houston still lives on a portion of the original land as does h
2 CONC er daughter Linda Houston Harper who married Jack R. Harper and grandso
2 CONC n John Houston Harper born in 1982. John became the 6th generation to l
2 CONC ive on his ancestors' land since it was acquired in McCracken County in t
2 CONC he early 1800s.  Submitted by Marion Houston.
