2 CONT WFT 137 # 299:
2 CONT History and Families of McCracken County, KY 1824-1989 on Fayette Harri
2 CONC son
2 CONT
2 CONT Fayette's son, W. D. Harrison born October 1844 served in the Civil War
2 CONC .  He was married June 19, 1879 to Mallie E. Hopson of Paducah, daughte
2 CONC r of George and Nellie Enders Hopson.  Her father was a native of Trigg C
2 CONC ounty, Kentucky.  IN 1880 W.E. purchardsed 283 acres of land in Ballard c
2 CONC ounty and moved there to rear his family.  W.D. was a successful farmer
2 CONC , acquiring several hundred acres of land, part of church and cemetery.  T
2 CONC o this union were born eight children:  Mary Emma married to Gillum Aus C
2 CONC handler; Jackson Fayette married Lola Mae Elrod; Angie M. married Georg
2 CONC e Cook; Lucille married Lex Ragland; Jennie, Louis, Elbridge and Antoin
2 CONC ette.  W.D., and Mallie werePresbyterians and W.D.  cast his first pres
2 CONC idential vote for H. Seymour in 1868.  (submitted by Howard E. Randle, g
2 CONC randson of Gillum Aus and Mary Emma Harrison Chandler and the great gre
2 CONC at grandson of Fayette Harrison).
