1 NOTE Histories and Families of McCracken County, Kentucky (1989; obtained fr
2 CONC om the Trewolla Moskop Haas Mansfield Tree):
2 CONT
2 CONT GILLUM AUS CHANDLER, born in Graves Co., KY, Apr. 28, 1879, married Mar
2 CONC y Emma Harrison in 1904.  Mary was born Feb. 28, 1881 to Wm. Davis Harr
2 CONC ison and Mallie E. Hobson of Ballard Co., KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aus' father, Alex Chandler, a farmer of Graves Co., KY was born in Nort
2 CONC h Carolina, came to Kentucky, married Amanda, a Kentuckian by birth.  T
2 CONC o this union was born J. Thomas, Joel, Oscar, Gillum Aus, Nora, Lillie a
2 CONC nd Wendell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nora married 1st Harvey Farmer, 2nd Mr. Bell; Lillie married 1st John M
2 CONC cDonald, 2nd Mr. York; Wendell married Belle Harris, one son Rev. Frank E
2 CONC lmo Chandler, who married Anna Bell Stokes and Oscar married Rebecca E. B
2 CONC ond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aus and Mary had four children: Robert Harrison who married Lillian Cop
2 CONC eland, daughter of Berry Paul Copeland Sr. and Willie Lynn Byrd of Mayf
2 CONC ield, KY; Mary Lillian who married Howard E. Randle Sr., one child Howa
2 CONC rd E. Jr., who married Louise Mason daughter of Dabner Rhea Mason and C
2 CONC arrie Norene Wolfe of Todd Co., KY; and James Burnly (Jim Buck) and Tho
2 CONC mas Moses Chandler were not married.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aus was a successful Paducah merchant and owned property in McCracken a
2 CONC nd Ballard Co., KY.  He served in the Spanish-American War, 39th Volunt
2 CONC ary Infantry.  Aus was only 15 when he enlisted, according to the story h
2 CONC anded down through the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Chandler died at their home Feb. 7, 1942 and Aus died at home Aug. 2
2 CONC 4, 1944.  Mr. and Mrs. Chandler are buried at Mt. Pleasant Baptist Chur
2 CONC ch Cemetery in Ballard Co., KY.  Submitted by grandson <i>Howard E. Ran
2 CONC dle Jr.</i>
