1 NOTE Batesville, AR, Daily Guard (obtained from Find A Grave, listing for Do
2 CONC ra Elizabeth Willis Breshears):
2 CONT
2 CONT MARSHALL, Mo. – Dora Elizabeth Breshears, 95, of Marshall, Mo., died Th
2 CONC ursday, Sept. 19, 2002, in Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Oct. 6, 1906, in Jasper, she was the daughter of Osbourne Hardy Wi
2 CONC llis and Laura S. Byrd Willis.  On Aug. 2, 1926, she married James Monr
2 CONC oe Davis, who preceded her in death Aug. 6, 1941.  On Jan. 31, 1953, sh
2 CONC e married Lester J. Breshears, who preceded her in death July 15, 1970.  S
2 CONC he lived in Marshall since 1947 after moving from Arkansas.  She was a h
2 CONC omemaker and a baby sitter for many years and a member of First Assembl
2 CONC y of God Church in Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include two daughters, Mary Gertrude Davis and husband Willia
2 CONC m of rural Napton, Mo., and Laura Ostler and husband Wally of Fresno, C
2 CONC alif.; a foster son, Marvin Lee Hunt and wife Barbara of Marshall; 10 g
2 CONC randchildren; 2 foster grandchildren; 16 great-grandchildren; 2 foster g
2 CONC reat-grandchildren; 12 great-great-grandchildren; several nieces and ne
2 CONC phews; a daughter-in-law, Veda Davis of rural Marshall; and a sister-in
2 CONC -law, Dorothy Willis of Lawrence, Kan.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents, her first husband, her second h
2 CONC usband, five brothers, five sisters and two sons, Marvin Davis and John H
2 CONC . Davis.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will be at 2 p.m. Saturday at First Assembly of God Church i
2 CONC n Marshall with the Rev. Dale Bean and William W. Harlow officiating.  N
2 CONC orma Eddy and Scottie Davis will sing “In the Garden” and “When He Reac
2 CONC hed Down His Hand.”  Leonda Raines, pianist and soloist, will sing “Ama
2 CONC zing Grace.”  Burial will be in Sunset Gardens Cemetery at Marshall wit
2 CONC h arrangements by Campbell-Lewis Funeral Home of Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers will be Chuck Davis, Marvin Leonard Davis, Rob Davis, Conny A
2 CONC hrens, Harold Eddy and Jimmy Willis.
