1 NOTE Note that Gervas William Davis and Mary Gertrude Davis were first cousi
2 CONC ns, but not by blood because she is a step-daughter to James Monroe Dav
2 CONC is.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marshall Democrat-News, 30 May 2006 (obtained from Find A Grave, listin
2 CONC g for Gervas William Davis, Sr):
2 CONT
2 CONT G. William Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT G. William Davis, 96, of rural Napton, died Friday, May 26, 2006, at Fi
2 CONC tzgibbon Hospital in Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. Wednesday, May 31, at Smith Cha
2 CONC pel United Methodist Church in rural Napton.  Rev. Doug Franklin will o
2 CONC fficiate. Pallbearers will be Rob Davis, Brian Schmidt, Roger Feagan, T
2 CONC ad Davis, Michael Martin, Darrell Ahrens, Joe Davis Jr. and Heath Thomp
2 CONC son.  Honorary pallbearers will be Bill Stouffer, Mavin L. Davis, Bill W
2 CONC erneke, Carter Shannon, Charles O'Neal, Marion Arni, J.L. Pulliam, Marv
2 CONC in Lee Hunt and Monte Holder.  Visitation will be held from 6:30 to 8 p
2 CONC .m. Tuesday, May 30, at Campbell-Lewis Funeral Home in Marshall.  Buria
2 CONC l will be in Smith Chapel Cemetery.  Memorials are suggested to Smith C
2 CONC hapel United Methodist Church or Smith Chapel Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Nov. 6, 1909, in rural Napton, he was the son of the late Joseph B
2 CONC . Davis and Ollie May Adams Davis.  On April 16, 1940, in Mountain Home
2 CONC , Ark., he married Gertrude Davis, who survives of the home.  He had li
2 CONC ved on the Davis family farm in rural Napton his entire life, where he w
2 CONC as a dairy farmer and an active member in the community.  He was a grad
2 CONC uate of Napton High School and had served on the Napton school board fo
2 CONC r many years.  He was a lifetime member of Smith Chapel United Methodis
2 CONC t Church, where he was very active and had held various positions in th
2 CONC e church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional survivors include his children: G. William "Bill" Davis Jr. a
2 CONC nd wife Patricia of Grand Rapids, Minn., M. Carolyn Jiles of Richmond, I
2 CONC nd., and Charles E. Davis and wife Joyce of rural Napton; one sister, M
2 CONC ary Catherine Garnett of Mexico; five grandchildren, Laura Zimmermann, D
2 CONC avid William Davis and wife Tracy, Andy Davis and wife Wendy, Kristan J
2 CONC iles and Tammy Lambrecht; five great-grandchildren, Logan Davis, Cooper D
2 CONC avis, Dustin Davis, Olivia Lambrecht and Wyatt Lambrecht; two step-grea
2 CONC t-grandchildren, Kris Lambrecht and Shane Lambrecht; and several nieces a
2 CONC nd nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by three brothers, J
2 CONC . Samuel Davis, Joseph B. Davis and Smith Davis, two sisters, Annis Dav
2 CONC is and Mattie Davis Feagan, and one brother in infancy.
