2 CONT
2 CONT Mary C. Garnett
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Catherine Garnett, 96, of Slater, died Sunday, Feb. 18, 2007, at H
2 CONC eritage Hall in Centralia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 10:30 a.m., Wednesday, Feb. 21, 2007, a
2 CONC t Smith Chapel United Methodist Church near Marshall.  Visitation will b
2 CONC e held from 6 to 7:30 p.m. Tuesday at Campbell-Lewis Funeral Home in Ma
2 CONC rshall.  Burial will be in Rehoboth Cemetery, near Slater. Memorials ma
2 CONC y be made to First Presbyterian Church of Slater, Smith Chapel United M
2 CONC ethodist Church or Rehoboth Cemetery.  Online condolences may be sent t
2 CONC o www.campbell-lewis.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Jan. 24, 1922, in Naptson, she was the daughter of the late Joseph B
2 CONC . Davis and Ollie May Adams Davis.  On Feb. 28, 1935, she married Willi
2 CONC am I. Garnett, who preceded her in death on Sept. 26, 1991.  She had li
2 CONC ved in the Slater area most of her life and was a homemaker.  She was a g
2 CONC raduate of Marshall High School.  She was a member of the First Presbyt
2 CONC erian Church in Slater and a former member of the Slater Garden Club.  S
2 CONC he enjoyed gardening and flower gardens.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include one daughter, Julia Ann" Judy" Garnett Martin of Thom
2 CONC pson; four grandchildren; 14 great-grandchildren; and several nieces an
2 CONC d nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents and husband, she was preceded in death by a d
2 CONC aughter, Eleanor Irene Garnett Schmidt; a granddaughter; four brothers, t
2 CONC wo sisters; and one brother in infancy.
