2 CONT The Examiner
2 CONT June 22, 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth D. Lane
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth D. Lane, 80, Shell Knob, Mo., died Tuesday, June 20, 2000, at h
2 CONC er home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Lane was born June 14,1920, in Independence. On Aug. 12, 1939, she m
2 CONC arried Oliver L. Lane in Olathe, Kan. She attended school in Independen
2 CONC ce, graduating from William Chrisman High School. She was a legal secre
2 CONC tary for law firms in the Independence and Kansas City area before movi
2 CONC ng to Shell Knob in 1974. She was a member of the Shell Knob United Met
2 CONC hodist Church, where she helped prepare the church bulletins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her survivors include her husband, Oliver L. Lane of the home; a son an
2 CONC d daughter-in-law, William and Linda Lane, Blue Springs; two sisters, M
2 CONC innie Licciardone, Old Forge, Pa., and Helen Rohman, Joplin, Mo.; and o
2 CONC ne granddaughter, Shelley R. Lane.
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside services will be 3 p.m. Friday at White Chapel Memorial Garde
2 CONC ns, Springfield, Mo. Arrangements are under the direction of the Willia
2 CONC mson Funeral Home, Shell Knob. 
