2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver L. Lane
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Lee Lane, 93, Independence, Mo., passed away Wednesday, Nov. 14, 2
2 CONC 007, at the Monterey Park Living Center.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver was born March 5, 1914, in Joplin, Mo., to Alan and Stella (Oman
2 CONC s) Lane. He proudly served in the U.S. Army Air Corps during World War I
2 CONC I. Mr. Lane retired from Standard Oil Refinery in 1974. Oliver and his w
2 CONC ife, Elizabeth, moved to Shell Knob, Mo., to enjoy 27 years of retireme
2 CONC nt fishing, boating and traveling. Mr. Lane loved his family dearly and w
2 CONC as a dedicated husband and father.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his son, William Lane and wife, Linda; and granddaugh
2 CONC ter, Shelley Lane. Oliver was preceded in death by his wife of 60 years
2 CONC , Elizabeth (Davis) Lane, in 2000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside services will be 2 p.m. Saturday, Nov. 17, at White Chapel Ce
2 CONC metery, Springfield, Mo. Online condolences may be expressed to the fam
2 CONC ily at www.speakschapel.com. Arrangements are under the direction of th
2 CONC e Speaks Suburban Chapel, Independence, 816-373-3600. 
