1 NOTE The Ochiltree County Herald (Perryton, TX), 30 Nov 1944 (obtained from F
2 CONC ind A Grave, listing for William Edward Tandy):
2 CONT
2 CONT Final rites were held Wednesday afternoon at 3:00, from the First Bapti
2 CONC st Church for W. E. TANDY, 62, prominent Ochiltree and Hemphill county f
2 CONC armer and stockman, who passed away at the Perryton hospital Monday eve
2 CONC ning, November 27.
2 CONT
2 CONT W. E. (Bill) TANDY suffered a stroke Saturday noon at his home 20 miles s
2 CONC outh of Perryton and was brought to the hospital Sunday night where he s
2 CONC uccumbed at 6:00 p.m. Monday evening.
2 CONT
2 CONT W. E. TANDY, son of Mr. and Mrs. Arch Henry TANDY was born October 9, 1
2 CONC 882 at Fort Worth.  He came to Ochiltree county in 1895 and was engaged i
2 CONC n extensive farming and stock raising.  He was a member of the Masonic L
2 CONC odge.  W. E. and Mrs. TANDY the former Golta KING, were in charge of th
2 CONC e Notla post office for two years until it was discontinued about a mon
2 CONC th ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. O. C. Curtis pastor of the Baptist Church held the services.  Two s
2 CONC ongs, “Shall We Gather at the River,” and “Rock of Ages” were sung by M
2 CONC r. and Mrs. A. K. Wooten, Mr. and Mrs. Robert Lawrence, Mr. and Mrs. Ma
2 CONC rk Burton, Mrs. John Osterbuh, Mrs. G. D. Holt, K. E. McKneeley and Rev
2 CONC . Elmer Holt accompanied by Mrs. Elmer Holt at the piano.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial was made in Ochiltree cemetery with Boxwell Brothers in charge o
2 CONC f the arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Honorary pallbearers were W. B. LaMASTER, Sam HERGERT, Fred TURNER, L. F
2 CONC . WAGGONER, H. L. WILBANKS and Claude BOWEN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors are the wife, three sons, Roger, Perryton; A. H. Mangum, Okla
2 CONC homa; Wm. E., in the service overseas, and one daughter, Mrs. J. D. WRI
2 CONC GHT of Dallas, three sisters, Mrs. S. W. SCOTT, San Antonio, Mrs. C. W. C
2 CONC ONRAD, Boston, Massachusetts, Mrs. L. L. MORRISON, Canadian; and five g
2 CONC randchildren.
