2 CONT
2 CONT Canadian [TX] Record, 13 Jul 1961 (obtained from Find A Grave):
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Lacy TANDY, longtime resident of the Gem comm
2 CONC unity before moving to New Mexico a few years ago, were conducted at th
2 CONC e First Baptist Church in Canadian.  Rev. Joe Vernon, pastor of the chu
2 CONC rch, and Rev. Sanford Cole were in charge of the rites.  Burial was in C
2 CONC anadian Cemetery under the direction of Stickley Funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. TANDY was killed in an automobile crash near Alamosa, Colorado.  S
2 CONC he was 62 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Florence M. TANDY was born in Swisher County, Texas, on June 3, 1899  S
2 CONC he was married to Lacy TANDY, who preceded her in death in 1957.  The T
2 CONC ANDYs lived in Hemphill County from 1927 until 1943 when they moved to T
2 CONC ruth or Consequences, New Mexico.  Mrs. TANDY was a member of the Bapti
2 CONC st Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving her are one son, Walter TANDY of Boise City, Oklahoma; and th
2 CONC ree daughters, Mrs. C. B. (Mary Nan) OLIVER of El Paso; Mrs. Floyd (The
2 CONC lma Flo) ROSS of San Antonio; and Mrs. Gordon (Jane) SHYLOW of Alamosa, C
2 CONC olorado; one sister, Mrs. Nannie BECK of Tulia, and one brother, R. H. G
2 CONC AYLOR of Krebs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another daughter, Helen Joyce TANDY of El Paso, who was injured in the s
2 CONC ame accident in which Mrs. TANDY was killed, died Wednesday night at a P
2 CONC ueblo, Colorado Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers at the funeral services were Homer and Leonard SANDERS, Wal
2 CONC ton and Morris MOORE, Arleigh HOOBLER and M. H. SMITH, Jr.
