2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. CARY N. DUNLAP
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Margaret Chrisman Dunlap, widow of Dr. Cary N. Dunlap of Middlebro
2 CONC ok, died Sunday morning (May 31, 1959) in a nursing home here.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Rockingham County on July 4, 1868, a daughter of the la
2 CONC te Joseph and Jennie Giles Chrisman.  Mrs. Dunlap was a member of Bethe
2 CONC l Presbyterian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are one daughter, Mrs. Margaret Dunlap Wayland, Staunton; one s
2 CONC on, Francis M. Dunlap, Clifton Forge, four grandchildren and nine great g
2 CONC randchildren.  Her husband, Dr. Dunlap, passed away in 1916.
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral service will be held Tuesday morning (June 2, 1959) at 11 o'c
2 CONC lock in Bethel Presbyterian Church, conducted by the Rev. James Sprunt, D
2 CONC . D.  Burial will be in the adjoining cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Active pallbearers will be R. Vance McClure, Ollie Hamilton, Graham Mis
2 CONC h, Frank A. Wright, Aubrey Smith, H. Clark Rosen, George E. Arnold and L
2 CONC acy Hanger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Honorary pallbearers will be Dr. Charles F. Gaylord, W. W. Hamilton and d
2 CONC eacons of Bethel Presbyterian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body is at the Fred Henry Funeral Home where the family will receiv
2 CONC e friends this evening from 7:30 until nine o'clock.
