2 CONT
2 CONT William Tams, born March 13, 1794, was a native of Buralen, England; im
2 CONC migrated to America in 1820; settled in North Carolina, where he marrie
2 CONC d, in 1824, Mary Brownlow Purviance, of Fayetteville, a granddaughter o
2 CONC f Col. Wm. Purviance, of Huguenot descent, who settled in North Carolin
2 CONC a in 1763; was appointed colonel of militia for New Hanover county 1775
2 CONC -6, page 365, "Revolutionary History of the State, by J. S. Jones." His o
2 CONC nly living child, William Henry Tams, born 1824, at Fayetteville, North C
2 CONC arolina, was a Master of Arts of Princeton College before he reached hi
2 CONC s nineteenth year; and, after graduating in law at the University of Vi
2 CONC rginia, settled in Rockingham county, Va., where he married Marie Antoi
2 CONC nette, daughter of the distinguished jurist Judge Daniel Smith.
