2 CONT In 1853 his parents settled at Staunton, V.; here he received his early t
2 CONC raining.  In 1873 he graduated from the Virginia Military Institute wit
2 CONC h distinction.  After teaching military tactics and chemistry for one s
2 CONC ession, he returned to Staunton, and shortly thereafter entered the ser
2 CONC vice of the Augusta National Bank, becoming its cashier in 1880, which p
2 CONC osition he still occupies.  He has been active in municipal affairs, an
2 CONC d is at present chairman of the city council.  He married, Nov. 17, 188
2 CONC 0, Sue Lewis Frazier, born May 19, 1859, daughter of the late Hon. Will
2 CONC iam and Susan Massie Lewis Frazier, of Staunton, Va.
