2 CONT From Find A Grave:
2 CONT
2 CONT ATTACK IS FATAL TO DR. B. G. GREGG
2 CONT
2 CONT Veteran Physician of Florence Will Be Laid to Rest This Afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Florence, Aug. 7--(AP)--Dr. B. G. Gregg, 72, who had practiced medicine h
2 CONC ere for 43 years, died suddenly of a heart attack at his home today.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Marion, Doctor Gregg was one of the best known physicians o
2 CONC f this section.  He was treasurer of the Methodist church for 30 years, a m
2 CONC ember of its board of stewards for 40 years, a trustee of Epworth orpha
2 CONC nage and a member of the board of church extension of the South Carolin
2 CONC a conference, Methodist Episcopal church, South.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doctor Gregg is survived by a son, Ben G. Gregg; a daughter, Mrs. F. H. B
2 CONC arnwell, both of Florence; a sister, Miss Lizzie T. Gregg of Marion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 5 p. m. tomorrow at Central Methodist c
2 CONC hurch.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was local surgeon for the Atlantic Coast Line and Seaboard Air Line r
2 CONC ailroads and was president of the Woodstone Hunting and Fishing club.  D
2 CONC octor Gregg was a graduate of Mercer University and the University of t
2 CONC he City of New York.
