2 CONT Mrs. Barnwell was born in Florence, a daughter of the late Dr. Benjamin G
2 CONC . Gregg and Kate Smith Gregg.  She was a graduate of Mary Baldwin Colle
2 CONC ge of Staunton, Va. and a graduate of New York School of Music and Art.  S
2 CONC he had lived all of her life in Florence except for the past four years o
2 CONC f which she had lived at the Methodist Home at Orangeburg.  She was a m
2 CONC ember of the Episcopal Church of the Redeemer in Orangeburg.  She was a f
2 CONC ormer member of All Saints Episcopal Church and Saint John's Episcopal C
2 CONC hurch in Florence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a son, G. Henry Barnwell of Orangeburg; a granddaughter, M
2 CONC rs. Barbara Savoie of Lafayette, La.; and a grandson, Frank H. Barnwell I
2 CONC I of Orangeburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the Morning News, June 28, 1977
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave also says that she was a gifted violinist, the second viol
2 CONC in graduate of Mary Baldwin College.
