1 NOTE From Find A Grave (listing for Mary Reeves Word):
2 CONT
2 CONT DAUGHTER OF PIONEERS, WIDOW OF BARRISTER, DIES IN DALLAS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be conducted at 4 p.m. Tuesday at the Word reside
2 CONC nce at 3107 Ross avenue for Mrs. Mary Reeves Word. 83, member of a dist
2 CONC inguished Texas family and longtime resident of Dallas, who died early M
2 CONC onday at home. Dr. Graham Frank, pastor of the Central Christian Church o
2 CONC f which she was a member will officiate. Burial will be in Greenwood Ce
2 CONC metery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Word was the daughter of Reuben A. Reeves a officer in the Confede
2 CONC rate Army, one-time member of the Supreme Court of Texas and later Chie
2 CONC f Justice of the Supreme Court of New Mexico during the administration o
2 CONC f President Grover Cleveland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Niece of Roger Q Mills
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother, Sarah Mills Reeves was a sister of Roger Q. Mills the well-
2 CONC known statesman.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1868 she married Jeff Word, son of Col. Thomas J. Word an attorney w
2 CONC ell-known both in Mississippi and Texas. At the time of her marriage he
2 CONC r husband was law partner of Judge John H Reagan, another widely nown T
2 CONC exas [sic]
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon after their marriage Mr. and Mrs. Word came to Dallas where Mr. Wo
2 CONC rd long was prominent as a jurist and civic worker. He died nine years a
2 CONC go.
2 CONT
2 CONT Native of Palestine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Word was born at Palestine, where her parents settled when they mo
2 CONC ved from Kentucky to Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by three daughters, Mrs. William Caven, Mrs Louis Leftw
2 CONC ich and Mrs. Olive Titterington, all of Dallas; one son, Arthur Word of S
2 CONC t. Louis and a granddaughter, Mrs. Robert McClendon of Los Angeles, for
2 CONC merly Miss Mary Olive Titterington of Dallas
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers at the services Tuesday will be John C Robertson, George Ro
2 CONC bertson, Alex Camp, D.W. Bowser, F.F. Glenn, Will R. Wilson, Edward Rel
2 CONC sterline and Robert Thorburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on her death certificate (obtained from Texas Death Certificat
2 CONC es 1903-1982 on Ancestry.com) is Mary Reeves Word.  Cause of death was a
2 CONC rteriosclerosis.  Place of death was 3107 Ross Ave., Dallas, Dallas Co.
2 CONC , TX (home).  The death certificate also lists her parents as Reauben [
2 CONC sic] A. Reeves and Sarah Mills.
