1 NOTE From Find A Grave (listing for Thomas Jefferson "Jeff" Word, Jr):
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Jeff Word Dies of Pneumonia~
2 CONT
2 CONT Texas Jurist Ends Career of Fifty Years in Dallas~
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Jeff Word 74 years old, well-known Jurist of Texas, who had been i
2 CONC n Dallas fifty years, died at his residence, ---- Ross Avenue at 10:15 o
2 CONC 'clock Wednesday morning.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had not been in the best of health, but was able to walk from the bu
2 CONC siness district to his home Saturday. The exertion is believed to have b
2 CONC rought illness which developed into pneumonia on Monday morning. His co
2 CONC ndition was not thought serious until early Wednesday when he began sin
2 CONC king rapidly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Word was born in Holly Springs, Miss. Nov 14, 1848. With his fath
2 CONC er Thomas Jeff Word, he moved to Texas a few years later, where the fam
2 CONC ily settled at Palestine. He married Miss Mary Reeves daughter of Judge R
2 CONC uben A. reeves and niece of Roger Q. Mills.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a young man he began a brilliant law practice as the partner of Judg
2 CONC e John H. Reagan of Palestine. After moving to Dallas he continued gene
2 CONC ral practice until a few years ago when his partner her [sic] Judge J.W
2 CONC . Thompson died. Since that time Judge Word had specialized in civil ma
2 CONC tters.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife, one son, Arthur Word of St. Louis. Three da
2 CONC ughters; Mrs. Louise Leftwich of Carlsbad, N.M., Mrs. William Cavin and M
2 CONC rs. Olive Titterington of Dallas and a granddaughter Olive Titterington
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Word was one of the oldest practicing attorneys in Dallas and was a m
2 CONC ember of the Central Christian Church. Funeral services will be held at t
2 CONC he residence at 4 o'clock Thursday afternoon, and will be in charge of D
2 CONC r. Graham Frank. At Greenwood Cemetery Masonic burial services will be h
2 CONC eld.
