2 CONT LOUIS C. LEFTWICH FATALLY WOUNDED
2 CONT
2 CONT FORMER DALLAS COTTON MAN ACCIDENTALLY SHOT AT CARLSBAD, N.M.
2 CONT
2 CONT CARLSBAD, N. M., March 25.-- Louis C. Leftwich, a leading cotton buyer o
2 CONC f the Pecos Valley, formerly of Dallas, died this morning at 6 o'clock a
2 CONC s a result of an accidental shooting Friday afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Leftwich was preparing to go fishing with another cotton buyer and i
2 CONC n getting some fishing tackle off a shelf in the sleeping porch pulled o
2 CONC ff a pistol, which was entangled in the fishing lines.  The gun caught o
2 CONC n a lower shelf and was discharged, the shot passing through the abdome
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Leftwich was taken to St. Francis Hospital, where an operation was p
2 CONC erformed.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Masonic service was held this afternoon before the body was taken to D
2 CONC allas for burial.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Leftwich was a 32° Mason and a Shriner.  His brother, Will Leftwich
2 CONC , manager of the Southland Hotel in Dallas, and Mrs. Leftwich's sister, a
2 CONC lso of Dallas, are here and accompanied the body to Dallas.
