2 CONT <b>Obituary notice from the Calgary Herald, Tuesday, February 26, 1980, P
2 CONC age C5:</b>  Hannah Ann Long died February 24, 1980 aged 87 years, form
2 CONC erly of King Tower.  Surviving are a son, Elliott, a step-son, Nelson; n
2 CONC ine grandchildren, sixteen, great-grandchildren, all of Calgary; sister
2 CONC s and brothers in the United States.  She was predeceased by her husban
2 CONC d, Frank in August 1964; a step-son Lester in 1967; a step-daughter, Ed
2 CONC na Mae Coleman in 1979.  Services at "The Little Chapel on the Corner" (
2 CONC JACQUES Funeral Home) Thursday at 1:00 p.m. Internment, Mountain View M
2 CONC emorial Gardens.  In lieu of flowers, if friends desire, donations may b
2 CONC e made to the charity of their choice.  Aunt Hannah fell while walking a
2 CONC nd broke her hip.  She contracted pneumonia and died from that.  Hannah w
2 CONC as somewhat forgetful in her later years while living alone so her fami
2 CONC ly put her in an adult care facility to be looked after.
