2 CONT
2 CONT Ernest Arthur Reeves, age 85 years of Centralia, Missouri died June, 10
2 CONC , 1989 at Boone Hospital Center, Columbia, Missouri.  He was born Augus
2 CONC t 21, 1903 in Howard County, Missouri the son of Charles Payne and Nanc
2 CONC y Catherine Ewins Reeves.  On April 12, 1932 he was married in Columbia
2 CONC , Missouri to Ila Roberts and she survives at the home.  Other survivor
2 CONC s are two sons, Larry Reeves, Centralia; Lonnie Reeves, Hallsville, fou
2 CONC r daughters, Lorna Fay Spires, Columbia; Shirley Gilmore, Hallsville; N
2 CONC elda Bosch, Columbia; Cheryl Bohlen, Okinawa, Japan; three brothers, Be
2 CONC njamin H. Reeves, Sheldon, Iowa; Owen W. Reeves, Sr., Brashear, Missour
2 CONC i; Woodrow W. Reeves, Centralia; twenty-one grandchildren and twelve gr
2 CONC eat-grandchildren.  He was preceded in death by a son, Charles Dee Reev
2 CONC es, one daughter, Iris Jean Moon, one grandson, Ronald Wayne Reeves, th
2 CONC ree brothers, Otha Bryan Reeves, William Thomas Reeves, Charles Reeves; t
2 CONC hree sisters, Hannah Ann Long, Martha Georgia Muzzy and Mary Edna Sarli
2 CONC s.  He was a member of the First Christian Church, Harrisburg, Missouri
2 CONC .  Mr. Reeves was a retired farmer and former employee of the City of C
2 CONC entralia.
