2 CONT <b>From the Sheldon IA Mail-Sun, August 20, 1997:</b>  Benjamin H. Reev
2 CONC es, 88, formerly of Sheldon, died Tuesday, Aug. 19, at the Carroll Heal
2 CONC th Center.  Services will be 10:30 a.m. Friday, Aug. 22, at First Refor
2 CONC med Church in Sheldon, with the Rev. Gordon Bloemendaal officiating.  B
2 CONC urial will be at East Lawn Cemetery in Sheldon, under the direction of V
2 CONC ander Ploeg Funeral Home in Sheldon.
2 CONT
2 CONT <b>From the Daily Times Hearold, August 20, 1997:</b>  Ben H. Reeves A f
2 CONC uneral service for Ben H. Reeves of Carroll will be held 10:30 a.m. Fri
2 CONC day, Aug. 22, 1997, at First Reformed Church in Sheldon.  Mr. Reeves, 8
2 CONC 8, formerly of Sheldon, died Tuesday, Aug. 19, 1997, at Carroll Health C
2 CONC enter.  The Rev. Gordon Bloemendaal will officiate the service.  Burial w
2 CONC ill be in East Lawn Cemetery at Sheldon.  Friends will call after 2 p.m
2 CONC . and the family will be present from 7 to 8:30 p.m. Thursday at Vander P
2 CONC loeg Funeral Home in Sheldon.  He was born Nov. 15, 1908, at Harrisburg
2 CONC , Mo., a son of Charles and Nancy (Ewens) Reeves, grew up in Missouri a
2 CONC nd moved to Sheldon at age 18.  He and Nellie Douma were married Dec. 8
2 CONC , 1937, at Sheldon.  They farmed near Sheldon and Hartley until 1970, w
2 CONC hen he retired and moved into Sheldon.  They moved to Carroll Health Ce
2 CONC nter in March 1993.  Mrs. Reeves died Oct. 12 of that year.  Mr. Reeves w
2 CONC as a member of First Reformed Church in Sheldon.  Survivors include two s
2 CONC ons: David Reeves and his wife, Sandy, of Devil's Lake, N.D. and Dougla
2 CONC s Reeves and his wife, Ruth, of Glidden; four grandchildren: Robert and M
2 CONC atthew Reeves of North Dakota and Rhonda and Rebecca Reeves of Glidden; a g
2 CONC reat-grandson, Michael Reeves; five sisters-in-law: Julia DeHoogh of Sh
2 CONC eldon, Cornelia Douma of Sanborn, Althea Reeves of Centralia, Mo., and M
2 CONC ary Reeves of Brashear, Mo.; and a brother-in-law, Cornie DeHoogh, of S
2 CONC heldon.  Mr. Reeves was preceded in death by his parents; his wife, Nel
2 CONC lie; six brothers; and three sisters.
