1 NOTE From Find A Grave (listing for Mary Ellen Wammack Reeves):
2 CONT
2 CONT DALLAS -- Graveside services for Mary Ellen Reeves, 90, of Dallas are s
2 CONC et for 2 p.m. Saturday at Fairview Cemetery with Ronnie Quaid, minister o
2 CONC f Commerce Street Church of Christ, officiating.  Arrangements are unde
2 CONC r the direction of the Geo. J. Carroll & Son Funeral Home of Gainesvill
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Reeves died Jan. 20, 2005, at Baylor Hospital in Dallas.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born Nov. 27, 1914, in Oklahoma to Joseph and Effie Mae Richard
2 CONC son Wammack.  In 1933, she married H.G. Reeves.  She was a homemaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her son, Robert H. Reeves of Dallas; daughter, Carol A
2 CONC nn Miller of Houston; four grandchildren; nine great-grandchildren; and s
2 CONC ister-in-law, Kathryn Cannon of Gainesville.
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, H.G. Reeves on May 16, 1964.
