1 NOTE Find A Grave (listing for Jacob VanLear Davis) and his death certificat
2 CONC e say he was born in Virginia, but the censuses consistently show his b
2 CONC irth in Missouri.  William Caldwell Davis and his family moved to Misso
2 CONC uri in 1838, but it is possible that James and Charlotte, with Jacob, m
2 CONC oved later.  Not sure which is correct.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A portion of Jacob's will, dated 6 Jun 1918 (obtained from "Missouri Wi
2 CONC lls and Probate Records 1766-1988" on Ancestry.com):
2 CONT
2 CONT After the payment of all my just debts, funeral expenses and the Expens
2 CONC es of my last sickness, out of my Estate, I give, devise and bequeath a
2 CONC ll the property of which I may die seized and possessed, of whatsoever n
2 CONC ature or description or wherever situate, real, personal and mixed, to m
2 CONC y beloved wife, Gustavia and to my children, James B. Davis, A. Mamie [
2 CONC ?] Brown, widow of Edwin Brown, deceased, Nellie V. L. Irwin [?], wife o
2 CONC f Charles J. Irwin [?], Eva J. Herring, wife of Lloyd Herring, and Jaco
2 CONC b B. L. Davis, equally, share and share alike.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on his death certificate is Jacob V. L. Davis.  Place of death i
2 CONC s given as Marshall, Saline Co., MO.  Cause of death given as lobar pne
2 CONC umonia.
