2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. John Angel, the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Wickersham, was born in S
2 CONC aline County, Missouri, May 7th, 1861, and passed away in Tipton on Sun
2 CONC day evening, May 10th, 1936, after a severe heart attack.  She had arri
2 CONC ved at the age of seventy-five years.  Her father died when she was a l
2 CONC ittle girl.  Her mother remarried.  Mrs. Angel was married in young wom
2 CONC anhood to a Mr. Davis.  They had lived in Saline county, Missouri, unti
2 CONC l after her husband's death.  On March 9, 1925, she was married to Mr. J
2 CONC ohn Angel and they located in Tipton, living here ever since.  In early w
2 CONC omanhood she became a Christian and united with the Methodist Episcopal C
2 CONC hurch South and was very active in the church.  When she came to Tipton s
2 CONC he transferred her membership to our Methodist Episcopal church.  She l
2 CONC eaves to mourn her passing, the husband, John Angel of Tipton.  She has t
2 CONC wo half-brothers, William and Cliff Hammond of Kansas City, and one hal
2 CONC f- sister, Mrs. Joe Settles of Sedalia, Missouri.  She has three sons b
2 CONC y her first marriage.  They are Walter Davis of Marshall, Missouri; Har
2 CONC ry Davis of Huntington, West Va.; and Ben Davis of Tulsa, Oklahoma.  Th
2 CONC ere are four grandchildren and one great-grandchild.  She was a good wo
2 CONC man and kind, and she had many friends.  Funeral services were held Thu
2 CONC rsday afternoon at the Fred Wilson funeral parlors, with Rev. Roscoe C. J
2 CONC errell in charge of the service.  Mrs. J. E. Chamberlain and Mrs. P.M. H
2 CONC offman sang two numbers.  The remains will be taken to Marshall, Mo. Fo
2 CONC r service and interment.
