1 NOTE From Find A Grave (listing for COL Frank Henry Barnwell):
2 CONT
2 CONT FLORENCE - Florence realtor Frank Henry Barnwell of 810 Cheraw Ave. die
2 CONC d Saturday afternoon in McLeod Infirmary after an illness of several mo
2 CONC nths.  He was 74.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be conducted at 4 p.m. Monday in All Saints Episc
2 CONC opal Church by Rev. Lynwood C. McGee.  Burial directed by Stoudenmire F
2 CONC uneral Home, will be in Mt. Hope Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Barnwell, a retired US Army colonel and veteran of two world wars, o
2 CONC rganized and was commanding officer of Battery A, 263rd Coast Artillery i
2 CONC n the South Carolina National Guard in Florence after World War I.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born August 3, 1893 at Adam's Run, a son of the late Gabriel Hen
2 CONC ry and Elizabeth Thompson Marshall Barnwell.  He attended Charleston Hi
2 CONC gh School, Porter Military Academy and Clemson College.
2 CONT
2 CONT After attending Clemson, he served with the US Army Engineers on the Me
2 CONC xican border.  He was commissioned as a 2nd lieutenant after attending t
2 CONC he first officer's training camp at Ft. Oglethorpe, Ga.
2 CONT
2 CONT During World War I, Mr. Barnwell served in the 323rd Infantry, 81st Div
2 CONC ision and the 30th Infantry, 3rd Division in the Army of Occupation in G
2 CONC ermany.  He entered the real estate and insurance business in Florence a
2 CONC fter World War I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Barnwell was commander of the Nation Guard when the late Sen. Olin D
2 CONC . Johnston, took over the State Highway Department.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the 263rd Coast Artillery was activated into World War II in 1941, M
2 CONC r. Barnwell returned to active duty and rose to the rank of colonel bef
2 CONC ore retiring in 1945.  He became active in the real estate and insuranc
2 CONC e business again and was president of Frank H. Barnwell Inc.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a former chairman of the Florence County Democratic Party and ha
2 CONC d served of the Florence City Council.  He was a member of the City, St
2 CONC ate and National Association of Real Estate Boards and was a past presi
2 CONC dent of the Florence Board of Realtors.  He was a member of the Florenc
2 CONC e Lions Club, the Veterans of Foreign Wars, American Legion Fred H. Sex
2 CONC ton Post No. 1, and was a mason.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of All Saints Episcopal Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are the widow, Mrs. Jessie Gregg Barnwell of Florence; a son, G
2 CONC . Henry Barnwell of Orangeburg; two sisters, Mrs. Bessie Dargan of Flor
2 CONC ence and Mrs. Edith Tobin; and 2 grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the Morning News, February 18, 1968
