1 NOTE Staunton News Leader, 8 June 2010 (obtained from Find A Grave, listing f
2 CONC or Anne Noble Sims Smith):
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Noble Sims Smith died peacefully Saturday, June 5, 2010, at her ho
2 CONC me, Waverley Hill, in Staunton, in her 87th year.  She was born Sept. 2
2 CONC 9, 1923, in Savannah, Ga. Her father, Irvin Augustus Sims, died when sh
2 CONC e was a few months old; she, a brother and two sisters were raised by t
2 CONC heir mother, Dorothy Hubbard Sims.
2 CONT
2 CONT At an early age, her family moved from Savannah to Portland, Maine, whe
2 CONC re she spent her childhood years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She attended Mary Baldwin College during the war years, graduating with t
2 CONC he Class of 1945.  In her senior year, she was student government presi
2 CONC dent and the May queen.
2 CONT
2 CONT After college, she was employed by the Massachusetts Society for the Pr
2 CONC evention of Cruelty to Children in Boston, Mass.  There she met her fut
2 CONC ure husband, Dr. Herbert McKelden Smith Jr., who was there for medical t
2 CONC raining.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were married July 10, 1948, at the Church of All Saints-by-the-Sea o
2 CONC n Southport Island, Maine, and then returned to Staunton, where they ra
2 CONC ised a family and Dr. Smith practiced medicine until his retirement in 1
2 CONC 984.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband was incapacitated by a stroke in 1996, and she did not leav
2 CONC e his side until his death eight years later.  They were married 55 yea
2 CONC rs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Over the years, she participated in a number of local organizations, in
2 CONC cluding Trinity Episcopal Church, the Mary Baldwin College Alumnae Asso
2 CONC ciation and Augusta Garden Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her sister, Dorothy Sims Ryan of Falmouth, Maine; a d
2 CONC aughter, Emily Smith Talley and her husband, Stephen E. Talley, of Stau
2 CONC nton; a daughter, Dorothy Smith Childers and her husband, Robert A. Chi
2 CONC lders, of Anchorage, Alaska; and a son, Herbert McKelden Smith and his w
2 CONC ife, Diana Donnelley Smith, of New Canaan, Conn.  She also is survived b
2 CONC y grandchildren, Henry Sims Talley of Staunton, Emily McKelden Smith, w
2 CONC ho lives in Tsubame, Japan, and Anne Donnelley Smith of New Canaan; thr
2 CONC ee nieces; and a nephew.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may be given in her name to either the Mary Baldwin College E
2 CONC ndowment Fund, PO Box 1500, Staunton, VA 24402 or to Valley Conservatio
2 CONC n Council, 17 Barristers Row, Staunton VA 24401, her favorite charitabl
2 CONC e organizations.
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial service will be conducted at 4 p.m. Sunday, June 13, 2010, a
2 CONC t Trinity Episcopal Church, 214 W. Beverley St., Staunton, with the Rev
2 CONC . Paul Nancarrow officiating.
