1 NOTE WFT 137 # 299:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Courtenay Trewolla was born April 16, 1802 near Truro, Cornwall Co
2 CONC unty, England.  He was christened on November 27, 1803.  He married Eli
2 CONC zabeth Boase in the town of Penzance, Cornwall County, England on Janua
2 CONC ry 3, 1825.  She was from a prominent Cornish family and was born on No
2 CONC vember 21, 1804.  The family came to America in 1836. There is no recor
2 CONC d of the port they sailed from or the port where they landed. However, i
2 CONC t is presumed that they landed in Richmond, Virginia for it was the por
2 CONC t of entry for immigrants with destinations of Virginia or North Caroli
2 CONC na in 1836. One child, Maria, was born in 1835 and died on board during t
2 CONC he journey to America.  Her body was wrapped in a blanket, weighted and p
2 CONC ut overboard by sliding it along a plank into the sea.  The family firs
2 CONC t settled in a village called Young's X-Roads, 17 miles north of Oxford
2 CONC , North Carolina in July 1841.  John was apprenticed to a tailor in Eng
2 CONC land and followed the trade in North Carolina.  The migration to Wester
2 CONC n was in 1846.  Details of this journey were in two diaries kept by Joh
2 CONC n Courtenay Trewolla and his son, John Henry Trewolla.  John Courtenay T
2 CONC rewolla died on May 27, 1857 in Christian County, KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Group Sheet of John Trewolla & Margaret H. Pearce sent to me by J
2 CONC ames D. Wilks Jr. of Anaheim, California
